ar \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM. State of emergency. New Jersey and New York on high alert for flash floods with a nor'easter bearing down right now. Millions of Americans bracing for dangerous conditions at this hour. We're tracking it all.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS AND THE COVID VACCINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR QUESTIONS ANSWERED\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Kids and the COVID vaccine. As the FDA gets ready for their big decision, the big questions from parents this morning. Doctor Ashton is here with what you need to know.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEATING BURNOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP INFLUENCERS SHARE THEIR TIPS FOR PUTTING OUR PHONES DOWN\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Beating the burnout. Ahead of a safety hearing on Capitol Hill with TikTok, \uc2 YouTube\uc2  and Snapchat, this morning the world's top influencers weigh in when it comes to too much time on social media. What they're saying about stepping away from your screen.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEN WITH BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THEIR POWERFUL MESSAGE ABOUT PERSONAL HEALTH\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Together in pink. Meet the men with breast cancer...\par \par \uc2 AUBREY (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 I'm a thriver.\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I am a thriver.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 ...sharing their stories...\par \par \uc2 KENNETH TODD NELSON (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 When we see something, say something, feel something, share.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 ...pushing more men to take charge of their health.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL LANDESBERG (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 If my story touches one person, and it saves a life of even one person then it makes it all worth it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Their powerful messages for everyone.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEREK HOUGH LIVE ON GMA!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUNNING "DWTS" HORROR NIGHT\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And a thrilling night in the ballroom. Derek Hough is live on "GMA" after that terrifyingly terrific tango, breaking down spin, after spin, after spin. \uc2 NBA\uc2  star Iman Shumpert stunning the crowd on horror night with a perfect score. We're screaming for more, and as we say, good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, America. I hope you're doing well this morning. We are looking forward to talking to Derek Hough.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We sure are. And, and do you know the Shue-Bachs?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Very well.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah, me too. That's what Amy Robach and her husband, Andrew Shue call their blended family of five kids. They are here this morning to talk about their children's book "Better Together." It's all about the strength of a blended family. They do that so well.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) A beautifully blended family...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...they are.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211112ehaq00038\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MOST EXPENSIVE THANKSGIVING EVER? PRICES OF TRADITIONAL MEAL INGREDIENTS ON THE RISE\b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, NOR'EASTER\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, MALL, INVESTIGATION, LEE, GYPIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO KILLED IN IDAHO MALL SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EYEWITNESSES SPEAK OUT AFTER FATAL ATTACK\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, CHILDREN, BURGERT, WALKER, KRUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA PANEL TO VOTE ON \uc2 PFIZER\uc2  VACCINE FOR KIDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROLLOUT FOR AGES 5-11 COULD BEGIN BY END OF NEXT WEEK\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, CHILDREN, COLLINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIH DIRECTOR ONE-ON-ONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON TODAY'S FDA PANEL MEETING & GETTING KIDS VACCINATED\par \par \uc2 TESLA, ELECTRIC CARS, HERTZ, OHSMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TESLA JOINS THE TRILLION DOLLAR CLUB\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERTZ BETS BIG ON ELECTRIC VEHICLES WITH MASSIVE DEAL\par \par \uc2 MICROSOFT\uc2 , RUSSIA, HACKING, SOLARWINDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HACKERS TARGETING GLOBAL TECHNOLOGY SUPPLY CHAIN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 MICROSOFT\uc2 : RUSSIAN GROUP BEHIND "SOLARWINDS" ATTACK TAKING AIM AT CLOUD SERVICES\par \par \uc2 WORLD SERIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY BALL!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRAVES & ASTROS SET TO FACE OFF IN FALL CLASSIC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, HALLS, BALDWIN, SHOOTING, "RUST"\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, SHIPPING, SUPPLY, FELTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON'S NEW SHIPPING STRATEGY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ADDING PLANES, TRUCKS, WORKERS & MORE TO GET GIFTS DELIVERED ON TIME\par \par \uc2 CONTRACTS, CARTER, INSURANCE, THETFORD, CLARK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY ON VEHICLE SERVICE CONTRACTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BETTER BUSINESS BUREAU URGES CAUTION AFTER RISE IN COMPLAINTS\par \par \uc2 BOSTICK, LIGHTS, HALLOWEEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 NOR'EASTER, EAST COAST, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , VACCINE, KIDS, FDA, VOTE\par \par \uc2 THANKSGIVING, EXPENSIVE, PRICES\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And Americans are bracing for what could be the most expensive Thanksgiving ever. The holiday is just over four weeks away and if you're hosting this year, the supply chain strain and other factors are contributing to price hikes on everything from the dessert spread to the price of the turkey. The cost of the bird might hit a record high, so it's a good year to have a potluck Thanksgiving.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Okay.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) If you want to come to my house to eat, you're bringing something. How about that?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KIDS AND THE COVID VACCINE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Coming up, we have more on kids and the vaccine. Doctor Ashton is here to answer your questions about your children and the shot.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BEATING SOCIAL MEDIA BURNOUT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Also this morning, beating the social media burnout. Top influencers share their advice on how to overcome it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACHAEL RAY LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And Rachael Ray tells us about losing her home in a fire and where she's building a new one. And here she is in our studio. She did all that during the pandemic. It's great to see her. Much more with Rach. She's here live. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 AUBREY (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 Hi, my name is Aubrey (inaudible) from Gainesville, Georgia and I'm a thriver.\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. I am a thriver.\par \par \uc2 MARK (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 Happy breast cancer awareness month. Let's make a difference.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Let's do just that. Welcome back to "GMA." Glad to have you with us. And so happy to hear from those men, the people with breast cancer who we rarely, rarely hear about. Well, this morning we will have more stories from male breast cancer thrivers just ahead.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I'm looking forward to that, and I have a connection to that as well.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211112ehaq0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MEN AND BREAST CANCER MALE SURVIVORS COMING OUT OF THE SHADOWS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,126 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, NOR'EASTER\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, MALL, INVESTIGATION, LEE, GYPIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST TWO KILLED IN IDAHO MALL SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EYEWITNESSES SPEAK OUT AFTER FATAL ATTACK\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, CHILDREN, BURGERT, WALKER, KRUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA PANEL TO VOTE ON \uc2 PFIZER\uc2  VACCINE FOR KIDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROLLOUT FOR AGES 5-11 COULD BEGIN BY END OF NEXT WEEK\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, CHILDREN, COLLINS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIH DIRECTOR ONE-ON-ONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON TODAY'S FDA PANEL MEETING & GETTING KIDS VACCINATED\par \par \uc2 TESLA, ELECTRIC CARS, HERTZ, OHSMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TESLA JOINS THE TRILLION DOLLAR CLUB\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERTZ BETS BIG ON ELECTRIC VEHICLES WITH MASSIVE DEAL\par \par \uc2 MICROSOFT\uc2 , RUSSIA, HACKING, SOLARWINDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HACKERS TARGETING GLOBAL TECHNOLOGY SUPPLY CHAIN?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 MICROSOFT\uc2 : RUSSIAN GROUP BEHIND "SOLARWINDS" ATTACK TAKING AIM AT CLOUD SERVICES\par \par \uc2 WORLD SERIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY BALL!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRAVES & ASTROS SET TO FACE OFF IN FALL CLASSIC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, HALLS, BALDWIN, SHOOTING, "RUST"\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, SHIPPING, SUPPLY, FELTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON'S NEW SHIPPING STRATEGY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ADDING PLANES, TRUCKS, WORKERS & MORE TO GET GIFTS DELIVERED ON TIME\par \par \uc2 CONTRACTS, CARTER, INSURANCE, THETFORD, CLARK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW STUDY ON VEHICLE SERVICE CONTRACTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BETTER BUSINESS BUREAU URGES CAUTION AFTER RISE IN COMPLAINTS\par \par \uc2 BOSTICK, LIGHTS, HALLOWEEN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 NOR'EASTER, EAST COAST, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , VACCINE, KIDS, FDA, VOTE\par \par \uc2 THANKSGIVING, EXPENSIVE, PRICES\par \par \uc2 KIDS, COVID, VACCINE, \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , FDA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 MEN, BREAST CANCER, AWARENESS, SURVIVORS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We're going to turn now to our "Together in Pink" series for Breast Cancer Awareness Month with a special look at how it affects a group of people who aren't usually associated with the condition. We're talking about men. The \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2  estimates there will be nearly 3,000 newly-diagnosed cases of invasive breast cancer in men in the US this year alone. We met the thrivers that are coming out of the shadows to spread awareness.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Although male breast cancer may be rare...\par \par \uc2 MARK (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 My name is Mark (inaudible) and I'm a thriver.\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. I am a thriver.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...it can be severe. Roughly out of every 100 breast cancers diagnosed is found in a man.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR LARRY NORTON (ONCOLOGIST MEMORIAL SLOAN KETTERING CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 That's still a whole lot of people, and for those individuals it's extremely important, obviously, for their lives.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Meet thriver Kenneth Todd Nelson.\par \par \uc2 KENNETH TODD NELSON (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 I have to continue to tell this story so I can help save lives.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At 34 years old, his life turned upside down after an unexpected moment at a routine allergy checkup.\par \par \uc2 KENNETH TODD NELSON (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 He just happened to ask is there anything else going on, and I happened to mention the small bump. He said I think you're okay, but let's just get it checked out. Everything completely stopped.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While facing stage 2 breast cancer, Kenneth kept his condition private at first.\par \par \uc2 KENNETH TODD NELSON (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 When you go into this room with all these ladies and you're the only guy, that's something else that does something psychologically to you, too. Now, it's this stigma for me that's associated with it.\par \par \uc2 FRIEND (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Kenneth is extremely brave. He wants to help everyone, protect everyone. That's what he does with that loving heart and spirit of his.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR LARRY NORTON (ONCOLOGIST MEMORIAL SLOAN KETTERING CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 Many men that we've seen will ignore a lump in their breast for months to years and that increases the chance that the cancer cells will spread to other parts of the body, and when that happens then a cure is much less likely.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For Michael Landesberg, he was told if he didn't have a mastectomy he'd only have one year to live.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL LANDESBERG (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 I need to get well, I need to beat this. I need, I need to be around for my wife and my son.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In recovery with loved ones by his side, Michael's journey ahead includes pushing more men to take charge of their health.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL LANDESBERG (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 I realize the importance of being proactive and going for screening and going for testing because it may be the difference between life and death.\par \par \uc2 JAMIE LANDESBERG (WIFE OF MICHAEL)\par \par \uc2 I don't know of any other man that would be able to get through that and come out better.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both Kenneth and Michael now working with the Male Breast Cancer Coalition to break the stigma...\par \par \uc2 KENNETH TODD NELSON (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 We're taught to be tough, to be silent, to be quiet when we go through things and that's the opposite of what we need to do. When we see something, say something, feel something, share.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...and raise awareness that men can get breast cancer too.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL LANDESBERG (THRIVER)\par \par \uc2 If my story touches one person then it makes it all worth it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And we really appreciate them sharing their stories like this. And, Michael, this really hits close to home for both of us. My brother, Butch had breast cancer, thankfully he's doing well. I know it impacted your family.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And, and my brother Gene (ph) he had male breast cancer, as well. He's doing fine, as well, but knowing what he went through and saw, saw - seeing how tough it was on him, I went and got the test that, that, that checks and makes sure that you're not the hereditary genetics, and it came back negative so I'm very happy. They checked for the mutations, but it was scary because when you know someone in your family you're a little...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...scared about it for yourself, but it is worth it to do it. I'm so happy I did it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It's scarier to have it and not know that you have it...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Exactly.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...as opposed to getting it. I'm proud of you.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So get checked if you can.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) That's it.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Definitely.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Important story right there.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211112ehaq0003d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 COMMON GROUND ABORTION RIGHTS\b0\par\par\uc2 2,070 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, SMITH, SIMPSON, FORD, TEXAS\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Thanks for joining us. Tonight, what's often lost in the highly charged fight over abortion, the individuals and the barriers that so often limit their choices. As the Supreme Court prepares to hear arguments next week on the highly restrictive Texas law, ABC's Janai Norman met some women who are putting aside politics and trying to help.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) This community where you decided to bring Abide, why here?\par \par \uc2 CESSILYE R. SMITH (FOUNDER & EXEC. DIR. ABIDE WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 Why not here? The entire southern sector of Dallas, which is predominantly black and Latina community, the disparities are high. Heart disease, cancer, preterm birth, teen pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Here in south Dallas, Cessilye Smith sees an inequality all around her. So, when it came time to open her easy access clinic, Abide Women's Health Services, she wanted it to be here.\par \par \uc2 CESSILYE R. SMITH (FOUNDER & EXEC. DIR. ABIDE WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 Our little part of creating a better world and creating a better environment for the families is Abide. So, this is the waiting room/education space.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Her priorities, life and what she sees as its many forms.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Your stance on abortion isn't cut and dry.\par \par \uc2 CESSILYE R. SMITH (FOUNDER & EXEC. DIR. ABIDE WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 It's not. I sit in the gray. At first, it was a very lonely place to be. It's an area where you have to do a lot of work. It's an area that you have to hold space for people that think differently than you.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The growing fallout from that Texas law banning most abortions.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 The law makes abortions illegal after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 One of the most direct challenges to Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The conversation around abortion is often divisive, seen by both sides as right versus wrong.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Hands off our bodies.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, with all eyes on Texas after a controversial bill, which limits abortions as early as six weeks, and the Supreme Court days away from hearing arguments, Cessilye is part of a wave of people approaching the dialogue in a different way, not seeing the issue as black or white, but living in what they call the gray.\par \par \uc2 MONICA SIMPSON (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR OF SISTERSONG)\par \par \uc2 This is a bigger fight than just marching in the streets.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) More focused on the reasons\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 CESSILYE R. SMITH (FOUNDER & EXEC. DIR. ABIDE WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 We're not really listening to women that are faced with this decision.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26and the resources\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 AMY FORD (CO-FOUNDER & PRESIDENT OF EMBRACE GRACE)\par \par \uc2 The church should be one of the first places she runs to for healing and for hope.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26than just the hot-button issue itself.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Where do you stand on abortion?\par \par \uc2 CESSILYE R. SMITH (FOUNDER & EXEC. DIR. ABIDE WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 I wish that abortion wasn't a thing. I wish that women were not placed in a position where they felt that they needed to have an abortion.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) You say that the issue of abortion has been politicized. What's the opposite of that?\par \par \uc2 CESSILYE R. SMITH (FOUNDER & EXEC. DIR. ABIDE WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 The opposite of that is creating a culture of life. The health care system, the, the food insecurities, the lack of employment, housing inequities, there are so many systems that lead to death. And so when I think about abortion, I do believe it's an important topic, but it's not the only topic. It's not addressing the whole of, of humanity.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Cessilye spent years as part of the anti-abortion rights movement.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Do you find on that spectrum that you can be pro-life without being pro-life enough? Or you can be pro-anti-abortion rights without being pro-anti-abortion rights enough?\par \par \uc2 CESSILYE R. SMITH (FOUNDER & EXEC. DIR. ABIDE WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. That's where I sit. The moment I began to speak more about the racial disparities in maternal health care, the racism, is the moment that things changed for me within the movement. I walk hand-in-hand with people that are pro-choice, people that are pro-life. I want women, I want families, I want birthing people to be liberated. And I don't believe liberation comes from abortion. I believe true liberation comes from addressing all of the other factors that contribute to the statistics that we see.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RATES PER THOUSAND, BLACK WOMEN 27.1, WHITE WOMEN 10\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MATERNAL MORTALITY, BLACK WOMEN 3X MORE LIKELY TO DIE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Statistics that, here, are particularly stark. The life expectancy in this part of Dallas is 23 years less than just nine miles north. Nationwide, black women have both the highest abortion rates and highest rates of maternal mortality. They're three times more likely to die from pregnancy-related issues than white women. For Cessilye, those are numbers and systemic drivers that can't be ignored in the discussion around what it means to choose life.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 The goal of Abide is to support life from the womb to the tomb. What does that mean to you?\par \par \uc2 CESSILYE R. SMITH (FOUNDER & EXEC. DIR. ABIDE WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 From the moment a woman or a birthing person becomes pregnant and they come through our doors, or even before, we're supporting them. We're creating a space where families will come long after they have children, because they know it's a safe place.\par \par \uc2 MYKAYLAH HENDERSON (NEW MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Walking in, everybody was really welcoming, and it felt like home.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For MyKaylah Henderson, who became pregnant with her daughter Kai at 17, Abide quickly became a place to ask questions and quell fears.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What was it like for you when you first found out you were pregnant?\par \par \uc2 MYKAYLAH HENDERSON (NEW MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 It was like a rush of emotions. Sadness, fear. I never thought I'd be pregnant at 17.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Did you ever consider having an abortion?\par \par \uc2 MYKAYLAH HENDERSON (NEW MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 At one point, yes. I did.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What even made you consider that option?\par \par \uc2 MYKAYLAH HENDERSON (NEW MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 I was thinking if I can't really take care of myself in all the ways that I need to, I don't think I can take care of a child. Finally, I decided to get my life together, started working. I want to go to nursing school. So, that's what I'm gonna do.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) MyKaylah decided to have her child, and by her side throughout was her mom, Shawana Carter. She knows full well the challenges of being a young mother.\par \par \uc2 SHAWANA CARTER (MOTHER OF MYKAYLAH)\par \par \uc2 I think I was able or tried to convey to Kaylah that this is your choice. And I think because I lived it, it was different. And so I was able to remember (inaudible) and say okay, we gonna fight this thing together. Come on. We got a little girl to take care of. Let's go.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While the decision to have an abortion wasn't right for MyKaylah, she's quick to note she is pro-abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What do you think could be the lingering impacts of this law?\par \par \uc2 MYKAYLAH HENDERSON (NEW MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 I think other states are going to try to follow in Texas' footsteps, but at this point, I don't think they should. A lot of women feel like their choices are being taken away from them.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTORS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Abortion rights. Abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Across the country at the Women's March in Washington, DC\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 MONICA SIMPSON (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR OF SISTERSONG)\par \par \uc2 You all can come around.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \u8230\'20\'26that impact is something Monica Simpson is keenly aware of.\par \par \uc2 MONICA SIMPSON (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR OF SISTERSONG)\par \par \uc2 This is the most dire attack on our, on our lives, right now, in terms of abortion access in this country.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Monica runs the Atlanta-based group SisterSong, which is focused on what they call reproductive justice, and frontline in efforts to fight restrictive legislation like Georgia's own heartbeat bill.\par \par \uc2 MONICA SIMPSON (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR OF SISTERSONG)\par \par \uc2 We're looking at the right, the human right for an individual to be able to prevent or end pregnancies without shame and with dignity.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And for Monica, it's a conversation not only about legal right, but access and support.\par \par \uc2 MONICA SIMPSON (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR OF SISTERSONG)\par \par \uc2 It's not just thinking about will I have a baby or not. It's thinking about will I have enough money to take care of this child when this child gets here. It's about will I be able to have access to the health care that I need to be able to make sure that I'm healthy, as well as my children are healthy. It's thinking about all of those things.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Back in Texas, Amy Ford is focused on faith as resource for those confronting unexpected pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 AMY FORD (CO-FOUNDER & PRESIDENT OF EMBRACE GRACE)\par \par \uc2 I had an unplanned pregnancy when I was 19 and almost had an abortion. And I didn't feel like I had anyone to go to for support. One big thing is that I went to church my entire life, every single week, and why did I not, in that moment, think, you know what? I'm scared, I don't know what to do. Maybe I should go to church and ask for prayer, wisdom, guidance. But it was the last place I wanted to go to.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Amy founded Embrace Grace, which helps connect those with unplanned pregnancies with churches and find resources through more than 700 support groups around the country.\par \par \uc2 AMY FORD (CO-FOUNDER & PRESIDENT OF EMBRACE GRACE)\par \par \uc2 God has amazing, huge plans for you.\par \par \uc2 AMY FORD (CO-FOUNDER & PRESIDENT OF EMBRACE GRACE)\par \par \uc2 We want the church to be one of the first places a girl runs to, instead of the last, because of shame and guilt. That's true feminism, is you can have your baby and your dreams, too. You don't have to sacrifice your baby in order to achieve your dreams. And we can make sure that you don't have to walk through this alone.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) How do we get more people into the gray area, to come out of their corners and to find some way to meet in the middle when it comes to abortion rights?\par \par \uc2 AMY FORD (CO-FOUNDER & PRESIDENT OF EMBRACE GRACE)\par \par \uc2 Just finding the commonality. What all can we agree on? On one thig I feel like, for the most part we can agree on, is no one wants an abortion. You don't want an abortion, but you feel like you don't have a choice. So, what we can agree on is can we help her make an educated choice?\par \par \uc2 MONICA SIMPSON (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR OF SISTERSONG)\par \par \uc2 So, in order to bridge this divide, I think it's important for us to create a space where we can all sit at the table together.\par \par \uc2 CESSILYE R. SMITH (FOUNDER & EXEC. DIR. ABIDE WOMEN'S HEALTH SERVICES)\par \par \uc2 The gray area is where you can hold strong to your convictions. You can. But then you find a common goal that can end up benefitting everyone. The gray area is where the real work is. As long as we operate in extremes, we will continue to fight.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Our thanks to Janai.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Up next, comedian Dave Chappelle. Some argue he's gone too far.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020211027ehaq00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HIDDEN COSTS OF CANCER TREATMENT FROM LOSING INCOME TO BEING UNDERINSURED\b0\par\par\uc2 710 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EXTREME WEATHER COAST TO COAST\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, FLOODING, MUDSLIDES\par \par \uc2 STORM, RAIN, WINDS, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 COVID, VACCINE, KIDS, FDA, ROLLOUT, FAUCI\par \par \uc2 BESSER, VACCINATED, KIDS, PARENTS, MASKS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DEMOCRATS, INFRASTRUCTURE, ECONOMIC\par \par \uc2 FBI\uc2 , HATE CRIMES, SPIKE, GREENBERG, THOMPSON\par \par \uc2 DRAG RACE, CRASH, CROWD, KILLED\par \par \uc2 BRADY, TOUCHDOWNS, HISTORY, CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIMING THE STORM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS; GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM "FRIENDS"\par \par \uc2 "RUST", SHOOTING, PROP, BALDWIN, HUTCHINS, 911\par \par \uc2 MERRICK, SHOOTING, MOVIE SET, CHARGES, LIABILITY\par \par \uc2 TYLER, CANCER, "FRIENDS", TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 HALLOWEEN, HAUNTED HOUSE, DENVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 STORMS, WEATHER, SNOW, ATMOSPHERIC RIVER\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, CHILDREN, BESSER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA PANEL SET TO MEET ON COVID VACCINE FOR KIDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ROLLOUT FOR AGES 5-11 COULD BEGIN AS SOON AS NEXT WEEK\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, "RUST", SEARCH WARRANTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH WARRANTS RELEASED IN MOVIE SET SHOOTING INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW EYEWITNESS ACCOUNTS AMID QUESTIONS ABOUT SAFETY ON "RUST" SET\par \par \uc2 SUPPLY, CRISIS, BOTTLENECK, SHIPPING, JINDEL, USPS\par \par \uc2 CANCER, TREATMENT, COST, MACDONALD\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, we're gonna turn now to the hidden cost of cancer treatment. It's a devastating diagnosis that certainly takes an emotional toll on a patient and their family, but it can also take a financial toll as well.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIDDEN COSTS OF CANCER TREATMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FROM LOSING INCOME TO BEING UNDERINSURED\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Rebecca Jarvis has some ways to get some help as well as one woman's mission to provide that help for others.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When Eudora Ward (PH) started treatment for breast cancer in 2020, she went on disability at her job at a mental health agency.\par \par \uc2 PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I needed time to get my life together for chemo. I needed time for me.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But chemo wasn't the Michigan native's biggest hurdle. It was paying the bills while on disability and getting just 60% of her salary.\par \par \uc2 PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I became behind in my rent and my ego wouldn't let me reach out to anyone.\par \par \uc2 MOLLY MACDONALD (FOUNDER THE PINK FUND)\par \par \uc2 Patients are not prepared for a diagnosis and they're not prepared for the financial implications of treatment.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Molly MacDonald knows this first hand. Her own breast cancer diagnosis led her to start The Pink Fund, a national nonprofit that provides a financial bridge to breast cancer patients by paying their living expenses for 90 days. MacDonald says most patients have no idea about the hidden cost of breast cancer, like losing income during treatment or transportation costs like parking fees and gas.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIDDEN COSTS OF BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 MOLLY MACDONALD (FOUNDER THE PINK FUND)\par \par \uc2 So, if you live in a rural area in this country and you wanna go to a nationally known cancer center, you may have a two to three-hour drive. If you are in radiation treatment every single day, you're probably going to have to stay in a hotel.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Experts say another hidden cost, being underinsured. Many people choose insurance plans based on the lowest monthly premium, not on the deductible, co-pays or what will be covered during a health crisis.\par \par \uc2 MOLLY MACDONALD (FOUNDER THE PINK FUND)\par \par \uc2 Wigs, mastectomy bras, additional surgeries that might be elective and not covered by insurance.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO GET HELP\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But there are some ways to get help. First, MacDonald says speak to a financial navigator at your hospital or treatment center.\par \par \uc2 MOLLY MACDONALD (FOUNDER THE PINK FUND)\par \par \uc2 That navigator can sit down and look at your insurance plan and determine if they can optimize or change your insurance.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also, you can negotiate a payment plan with your provider. As for Ward, she applied for financial assistance from The Pink Fund, who paid two months of her rent and other living expenses.\par \par \uc2 PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It meant a lot because the last thing you wanna worry about while you're going through cancer is bills or money.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For "Good Morning America," Rebecca Jarvis, ABC News, New York.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) That is such an important story. I wanna thank Rebecca for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211112ehap0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HIGH COURT DEFERS ABORTION LAW ACTION REFUSES TO BLOCK TX LAW; SETS HEARING FOR NOV. 1\b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BALDWIN, SHOOTING, INVESTIGATION, HUTCHINS\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, BERNSTEIN, GRAY, WALENSKY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 : SHOT EFFECTIVE FOR KIDS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION LAW, TEXAS, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COURT DEFERS ABORTION LAW ACTION\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Next, the Supreme Court refusing to block the Texas law that has banned most abortions in the state. The Biden administration had asked the court to put the law on hold until legal challenges are resolved. So, let's bring in ABC's chief Washington correspondent, \uc2 Jonathan Karl\uc2 . And, Jon, in a highly unusual move, the court has agreed to an expedited review of this law in just ten days.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH COURT DEFERS ABORTION LAW ACTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REFUSES TO BLOCK TX LAW; SETS HEARING FOR NOV. 1\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Whit, this is the quickest review that the court has granted to any law, by far, since Bush v. Gore way back in 2000. The court will be looking strictly at that highly unusual mechanism that Texas put in place to enforce the law.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) As a reminder, here's how it works. The law gives any citizen the power to sue anybody that they say aids or abets an unlawful abortion, from the doctor who performs the procedure, to the Uber driver that drives a woman to the clinic. If they win, they would get a bounty of at least $10,000.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Justice Sotomayor, Justice Sonya Sotomayor has issued a dissent in this order, raising objections to the fact that the court hasn't immediately thrown out the law.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She wrote, quote, "Women seeking abortion care in Texas are entitled to relief from this court now. Because of the court's failure to act today, that relief, if it comes, will be too late for many."\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) But, Whit, it's important to point out that even conservatives on the court has raised doubts about the constitutionality of this Texas law.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And so many watching this case very closely. Jon, thank you.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Sure.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020211025eham00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ONE-ON-ONE WITH THE FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN ON BREAST CANCER SCREENING\b0\par\par\uc2 2,006 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MCPHERSON, LAUNDRIE, PETITO, BERTOLINO, SCHMIDT, BLUE\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, BOOSTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA AUTHORIZES MODERNA & J&J BOOSTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGENCY ALSO BACKS "MIXING AND MATCHING" VACCINE BRANDS\par \par \uc2 INFRASTRUCTURE, BIDEN, VOTING RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 PLEA, ESPIONAGE, TOEBBE, SUBMARINE\par \par \uc2 PLANE CRASH, INVESTIGATION, JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEARCH FOR ANSWERS IN FIERY PLANE CRASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW DID ALL 21 PEOPLE ONBOARD JET ESCAPE THE WRECKAGE?\par \par \uc2 WORLD SERIES, BASEBALL, \uc2 HOUSTON ASTROS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ASTROS TAKE ALCS GAME 5\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOUSTON MOVES ONE WIN AWAY FROM WORLD SERIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 "AMERICA'S GOT TALENT", GOODWIN, STUNT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "TO THE VERY BRINK"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUNTMAN BREAKS SILENCE AFTER TERRIFYING ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , RACE-NORMING, SETTLEMENT, LEONARD, HENRY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AN END TO THE USE OF "RACE NORMING"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: A SYSTEM THAT DENIED SOME BLACK FORMER NFL PLAYERS BIG PAYOUTS FOR HEAD INJURIES\par \par \uc2 AIRFARE, TRAVEL, GAS PRICES, KIRBY, ORLANDO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AIRFARES TAKING OFF\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNITED CEO WARNS OF HIGHER TICKET PRICES AS FUEL COSTS CLIMB\par \par \uc2 NFL\uc2 , SMOOT, SHATWAN, CHILDBIRTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 LAUNDRIE, PETITO, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , REMAINS, MCPHERSON, BERTOLINO\par \par \uc2 COVID, SPIKE, VACCINATIONS, UK\par \par \uc2 ROMANCE, SCAMS, FTC\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, BREAST CANCER, AWARENESS, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And now it's going to get to our "GMA" Cover Story. Robin, you had a chance to sit down with the First Lady.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I did. We spent some time yesterday in the Bronx. She has on - she's on a mission for Breast Cancer Awareness Month to encourage women to make a potentially life-saving appointment. Now during the pandemic, millions, millions have been missing all types of screenings. We spoke about her personal connection to this mission, as well as her dedication to being an educator as she has embraced for, for decades. Doctor Biden is devoted to using the power of education to deliver her message.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I know how much it means to you, the three initiatives that you are so passionate about, the military...\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...education, cancer awareness.\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Here you are, First Lady, education is still so important to you...\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...for you to be there at Northern Virginia Community College.\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 That's right, that's right.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) How are you able to balance all of that?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCTOR JILL BIDEN ON BALANCING LIFE IN THE WHITE HOUSE AND TEACHING\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I just wanted to continue teaching and I thought, why not? I'm there two days a week, I teach writing, and the other days I'm in my White House office, so it just works and it makes me so happy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And to be at a community college - and I don't have to tell you that some people are concerned with the social spending bill, that being that free tuition at community college may have to be taken out of the bill. For families that were hoping for that, what would you say to them?\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I would say we're not giving up, we are not giving up. This is round one, this is year one, I'm going to keep going.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also at the top of Doctor Biden's agenda as First Lady, breast cancer awareness...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCTOR JILL BIDEN ON BREAST CANCER AWARENESS\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Get your mammogram, it might save your life.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...now pushing for more women to get screened.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And you're saying there's nothing more important on your to-do list.\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 That's right. The next thing you have to do today is call your doc and get in there and get your screenings. If you go get that mammogram and they catch it early you have a fighting chance.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So for the folks who say, Doctor Biden, I'm too busy, I'm too busy.\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I'm busy too, but you know what, as soon as we got into office, there I was off and getting my mammogram. I think I got it within the first month. There's nothing more important than your health, nothing.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is personal for the First Lady who's been advocating for breast cancer research since the early '90s.\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I had four friends who were diagnosed with breast cancer at the same time. Unfortunately, we lost one of those friends and I was so upset and I thought, what could I do, there has to be something. So I thought I know education, you know, inside and out, and so let's start to educate people.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Here at the Montefiore Einstein Cancer Center, a team of doctors is working to prioritize breast cancer screenings as mammogram rates have dropped as much as 80 percent throughout the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Doctor Rivera, the work that you're a part of with the COVID cancer screening research, what is your research showing you?\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR AMANDA RIVERA (RADIATION ONCOLOGIST MONTEFIORE EINSTEIN CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 We screen about 41,000 patients, getting mammograms every year, and with the pandemic year, that dropped to almost 31,000. Yeah, that's disheartening and we really just want people to get their cancer detected early so that we have more treatment options.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) 52-year-old Sandra Cruz was hesitant last year and pushed back her annual mammogram. Her doctor urged her to get screened this past April, that's when she learned of her stage 1 breast cancer diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And radiation's going to begin shortly?\par \par \uc2 SANDRA CRUZ (RECENTLY DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) But what did you find out recently?\par \par \uc2 SANDRA CRUZ (RECENTLY DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER)\par \par \uc2 No chemotherapy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Oh, my goodness. So how are you feeling?\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 That's a blessing.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) That is, that is.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR AMANDA RIVERA (RADIATION ONCOLOGIST MONTEFIORE EINSTEIN CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 It's amazing (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 SANDRA CRUZ (RECENTLY DIAGNOSED WITH BREAST CANCER)\par \par \uc2 Well, I feel great, honestly. I was one of those woman during the pandemic that had the fear of coming and getting screened. I, for one, didn't know what COVID was all about, the fear of catching it, so I was one of those in individuals that waited until things calmed down.\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Now that we've moved on a little bit and people are vaccinated, we have to make sure that - we have to get the message out.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I believe that your first trip as First Lady was to Richmond, Virginia...\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...where you spoke about cancer, you talked about health care, you talked about the inequities. What is it that can be done to help level the playing field, if you will, when it comes to health care?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCTOR JILL BIDEN ON LEVELING THE PLAYING FIELD IN HEALTH CARE\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 It's the responsibility of the federal government to make sure that we have access - that all communities have access.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR AMANDA RIVERA (RADIATION ONCOLOGIST MONTEFIORE EINSTEIN CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 Communities where there's less access to health care, we have barriers to overcome in terms of getting that population in for cancer screening. When you add a pandemic onto that, those disparities only grow further.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And your research also includes looking at more diversity in clinical trials. Talk about why that is so important.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR AMANDA RIVERA (RADIATION ONCOLOGIST MONTEFIORE EINSTEIN CANCER CENTER)\par \par \uc2 Until we get more representation on those clinical trials we're not adequately assessing that patient population, so it's very important to get more clinical trial enrollment from, from communities of color.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) You have said going into next year, cancer efficacy, that there were things and issues that you want to work on dealing with this. Can you be specific in what you're hoping to do in the new year?\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I'm a member of a family who has - just like actually most American families - who have dealt with someone in their family...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yes.\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 ...with cancer. I know what it's like to sit in that chemotherapy room with your loved one and just, you know, holding his or her hand and just helping them to get through it, and it's important.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What would you want people to think about you as First Lady when it's all said and done?\par \par \uc2 FIRST LADY DOCTOR JILL BIDEN (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I would hope that people would say she saw us, she heard us, and she helped us heal as a nation.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) They saw us and helped us heal, that's how she wants to be seen. And like all families, her family very much impacted, her parents...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yep.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...cancer, her sister, of course Beau, and really with her four friends in 1993 were diagnosed all at the same time. And we've talked about this, we've had friends - and there's just virtually nobody who hasn't been impacted with some form of cancer and breast cancer happens for men, as well, my brother had breast cancer and is doing really well, so.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Nine months in, she seems still down to Earth.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Very approachable. She was late, which is fine...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It happens.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...(inaudible) which is real. But now, just the way that she, she carries herself and, and when she was talking about education and I, you know, I, I put it to her about the social spending package and community college. A lot of folks were, were planning on it being free and here she is a teacher, an - a professor at, at a community college in Northern Virginia. But didn't shy away from, from speaking about anything and really feels okay, this is round one, year one...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Mm-hmm.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...of the administration.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) There's time.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And I want people to know - and we - first of all, I hope that the woman that we interviewed, Sandra, the patient, we're wishing her all the best. And if you need help of getting any type of screening when it comes to cancer, you can call the Cancer Information Service, 1-800-4-cancer. It's on our screen, 1-800-4-cancer\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANCER INFORMATION SERVICE 1-800-4-CANCER (1-800-422-6237)\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Thank you, Robin. I liked when she said, I'm busy, too...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah. Yeah, we all do.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...if I have time to get screened, you can too, and that is so true.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) That's right.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211109ehal0000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DO YOU BUY THAT? NATE SILVER FROM FIVETHIRTYEIGHT\b0\par\par\uc2 591 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2021 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 HAITI, GANGS, MISSIONARIES, CHILDREN, KIDNAPPED\par \par \uc2 FAUCI, J&J, BOOSTER, FDA, MODERNA, \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , KIDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVID-19 THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA PANEL RECOMMENDS BOOSTER FOR J&J VACCINE\par \par \uc2 COVID, SUPPLY, SHIPS, LONG BEACH, LABOR, INFLATION\par \par \uc2 SWONK, SUPPLY, CRISIS, BIDEN, WORKERS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPPLY CHAIN GRIDLOCK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S BEHIND GLOBAL SUPPLY CHAIN CRISIS?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, BILLS, STRIKE, POLLS, TRUMP, JAN 6, FLAG\par \par \uc2 SILVER, 538, ANALYSIS, ABORTION, TX, VOTERS, POLLS\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court has allowed a state law to stand that deputizes citizens, anyone, to proclaim themselves in a position to have the right under law to interfere with those choices that that woman has made. The \uc2 United States Department of Justice\uc2  is prepared to take action and to sue.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  last month, and that near total abortion ban in Texas is now headed back to the Supreme Court, just the latest twist in a blockbuster court term that could determine the future of the constitutional right to an abortion and the outcome of the 2022 midterms. So, which voters could be more energy? FiveThirtyEight's Nate Silver analyzes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO YOU BUY THAT?\par \par \uc2 NATE SILVER (FIVETHIRTYEIGHT)\par \par \uc2 It's probably time to revisit some of our assumptions about the politics of abortion. The conventional wisdom is that while there are plenty of pro-choice voters and plenty of pro-life voters, conservatives are more likely to view abortion as a decisive issue for their vote. Back in February, for example, around 47% of Trump voters said abortion was a very important issue for them, as compared to 39% of Biden voters, according to polling from YouGov. But we've seen a big change since September 1st, when the Supreme Court allowed a highly restrictive Texas abortion law to remain in effect. In the most recent YouGov polling, about 51% of Biden voters described abortion as very important, as compared to just 36% of Trump voters.\par \par \uc2 NATE SILVER (FIVETHIRTYEIGHT)\par \par \uc2 That may be because voters get particularly motivated when you're potentially taking away something they thought they already had. The Texas law, for example, has been interpreted by experts as a signal that the Roe v. Wade decision could be overturned, a decision that remains quite popular often by two-to-one margins in the polls. A recent \uc2 Quinnipiac University\uc2  poll, for instance, found that 67% of voters generally agree with Roe v. Wade, as compared to 27% opposed. One can perhaps draw a parallel to Obamacare, which motivated Republicans in the 2010 midterms, because it reflected a change to the status quo.\par \par \uc2 NATE SILVER (FIVETHIRTYEIGHT)\par \par \uc2 But, by the 2018 midterms, when Obamacare was the law of the land, it had become fairly popular, and Republican members of Congress were punished by voters for their efforts to take it away. So, I want to be careful, here, both because of the sensitivity of the topic and because abortion is one of many issues that will effect the vote next year, but I surely do buy the Democrats will be motivated if they see Roe V. Wade as being under a threat.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Our thanks to Nate.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Coming up, our exclusive preview of MI6 spy \uc2 Christopher Steele\uc2 's interview, what he told George Stephanopoulos about Trump and Russia, next.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) The first look at George Stephanopoulos' brand-new documentary is next. Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020211025ehah00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WHITE HOUSE TO FIGHT TEXAS ABORTION LAW DOJ PLANS TO ASK SUPREME COURT TO INTERVENE\b0\par\par\uc2 131 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOOSTER BREAKTHROUGH\par \par \uc2 J&J, BOOSTER\par \par \uc2 BOOSTER, VACCINE, MIXING, OFFIT\par \par \uc2 TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 CLINTON, HOSPITALIZED, INFECTION\par \par \uc2 SUPPLY CHAIN, SHORTAGES\par \par \uc2 WHITE HOUSE, TEXAS, ABORTION, SUPREME COURT\par \par \uc2 VICTOR OQUENDO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And we turn now to the Texas abortion law. The Biden administration saying that it will fight the law, the most restrictive in the nation, taking the cause to the Supreme Court. That legal battle over Texas' law is fueling a public debate over the Supreme Court and its conservative majority. Friday, a commission appointed by President Biden to examine possibly making changes to the court, had their first public meeting, making their arguments about possibly expanding the number of seats on the court or instituting term limits.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211029ehag0005r\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS ABORTION BAN UPHELD FEDERAL APPEALS COURT REJECTS JUSTICE DEPARTMENT CHALLENGE\b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT CLINTON HOSPITALIZED\par \par \uc2 CLINTON, HOSPITAL, ICU, SEPSIS, ALI\par \par \uc2 VACCINES, BOOSTERS, FDA, BROWNSTEIN, MANDATES\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, VACCINE, TSA, AIRLINES, HARTEVELDT\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, COURTS, JUSTICE DEPARTMENT, TEXAS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yep, gonna have to be patient. Okay, Victor, thanks. We're gonna get the latest now on the Texas abortion law. It's the most restrictive in the country, and it's another step closer to the Supreme Court. A federal appeals court rejected the Biden administration's latest attempt to stop the law which bans most abortions. Rachel Scott is tracking the case. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION BAN UPHELD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL APPEALS COURT REJECTS JUSTICE DEPARTMENT CHALLENGE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) George, good morning. The Texas attorney general calling this a big win for the state, but this is not what the Biden administration wanted this morning. The fifth circuit, considered one of the most conservative appeals courts in the country, siding with the state of Texas, allowing the most restrictive abortion law in the nation to stand. This bans abortions as early as six weeks into a woman's pregnancy. That is before many women even know that they are pregnant.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And the last several weeks have been whiplash in Texas as this law makes its way through the courts. The next move is now on the Justice Department. But as you said, this does lay the groundwork for this challenge to reach the Supreme Court. And until a higher court weighs in, the reality for women in Texas is if they want an abortion, they'll likely have to travel out of state to get it, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Racheal Scott, thank you. Michael.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211029ehaf0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE APPOINTMENT JOURNEY, OF A YOUNG WOMAN SEEKING ABORTION CROSSING STATE LINES\b0\par\par\uc2 3,311 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 TEXAS LAW, ABORTION, GARDNER, ROSE, BREWER\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The clock is ticking, and this Texas college student can feel every second pass, like a lifetime.\par \par \uc2 JANE (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 So, you can just have a seat, right here.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 It's, like, I'm pregnant. I'm trying to get an abortion,\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For thousands in this state, these are desperate times.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Drowning is the best word to describe it is drowning.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Abortion rights battle playing out in Texas.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The legal back and forth of the highly restrictive abortion law.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Thousands protesting in cities across America.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, a deeply intimate journey, crossing state lines.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Now, it's a waiting game.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) From Texas, where a new law banning abortion at six weeks is pushing women to travel hundreds of miles.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 No one talks about this process.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) To Mississippi, where one clinic sits at the center of a Supreme Court case that could forever change the right to choose.\par \par \uc2 ACTIVIST (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 There aren't any laws on the books in any state regulating men's bodies. It's sexist. It's unequal, and it's wrong.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One young woman pulls back the curtain, revealing the lengths people will go, the hurdles they will jump, in order to have choice.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 My body is not their property.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 My name is Maddie. I am a senior in college. I just turned 21.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 They moved from it online lab to in-person lab, but I don't know where the lab is.\par \par \uc2 FRIEND (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Does it say?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I would say I'm a pretty typical college kid. Wake up, go to work or class, depending on the day.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Tell me a little bit about what's going on.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Well, I am 13 weeks pregnant, right now, and I'm not in a place to have a baby.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) You didn't plan to be pregnant at this period in your life?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely not. I was in a committed relationship, but things happened. It didn't work out. But I was on birth control. I didn't want a family.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I think people watching this may have the question of, if you were on birth control, how could you possibly be pregnant?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Birth control is not 100%. I had been not sleeping and not eating and nauseous for a few weeks. I thought it was just stress of life until I took one test, and it came out a clear plus sign, from the beginning, and I was devastated.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What was the point when you realized that you wanted to go forward with an abortion procedure?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I would say it probably took between two and three minutes of thinking before I knew that that was going to be my choice.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But this is Texas. In 2021, a new world, thanks to a new law called Senate Bill 8, which bans abortion as early as six weeks into pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) At six weeks, you didn't even know you were pregnant?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Not even close. I was still living my life as regular and as carefree of a college kid as I could be.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After several positive pregnancy tests, Maddie booked an appointment at Planned Parenthood.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 When she told me that I was measuring at 10-and-a-half weeks, I just cried. I was heartbroken and terrified. I immediately knew that any chance I had of being able to have this procedure done in Texas was gone. I started researching with the materials that Planned Parenthood gave me and looked into Louisiana, and Louisiana was booked out three weeks.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Three weeks?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Yes. I called Alabama and Kansas and Oklahoma and Vegas and Georgia and Tennessee.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) How many clinics would you say you called, altogether?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Easily 30, if not more.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The earliest appointment she could find, 400 miles away in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Did you realize the significance of that clinic?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 No. I honestly didn't find out until a friend said, did you know that that's the only clinic in Mississippi that's performing abortions?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jackson Women's Health isn't just the state's last abortion clinic, it's also at the center of a potentially historic case before the Supreme Court, a case that could dramatically reshape access to abortions nationwide.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 So, the Bible says...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Don't stand with the sinners. Go home.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And possibly to overturn Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREWER (CLINIC DIRECTOR JACKSON WOMEN'S HEALTH ORGANIZATION)\par \par \uc2 I think they've gone too far.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Shannon Brewer has been working here for 20 years. She's been the clinic director since 2010.\par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREWER (CLINIC DIRECTOR JACKSON WOMEN'S HEALTH ORGANIZATION)\par \par \uc2 The new Texas law is not deterring people from getting an abortion. We've been even busier because now we're seen seeing a lot more patients from Texas. We've almost doubled our capacity. Our phones are ringing nonstop because of this.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Maddie was one of those calls. And since she had to go out of state, she needed help. So, she reached out to her parents.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 It was like, okay, I'm pregnant. I'm sorry, because, at that moment, I felt like I was a disappointment.\par \par \uc2 PARENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 That was the farthest from the truth.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Maddie's mom asked not to reveal their identity, in order to protect their family.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) As a parent, what has been the most difficult part?\par \par \uc2 PARENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm angry. Not at her. I'm angry with Governor Abbott. I'm angry that men have decided this is what's best for women.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What message do you have for the Texas lawmakers who backed this law?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 My body is not their property. It's mine. I am in charge of myself, in every possible way.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEDNESDAY, DAY OF PROCEDURE\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I really didn't sleep, because my mind was just a wreck. There are so many emotions going on at once, that it was a blur. The anxiety was still there. The frustration was still there. The fear of the unknown. The drive that morning, I tried to keep it light.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:00 AM\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 And so, (inaudible) them.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:25\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Trying to keep as much pressure and stress off as possible. The entire flight, I was trying not to cry.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 9:25 AM\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I had to keep in mind that I was doing this for me. This is my future on the line. It's my body on the line. It's a lot to take in.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 11:00 AM\par \par \uc2 CABIN CREW (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Welcome to Jackson.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MISSISSIPPI\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 It still feels nice, out here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 1:00 PM\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I was very fortunate when I showed up to the Women's Health. There were only a few protesters. And that's when it started to get a little bit heavier and more real. The minute that I walked into the clinic, I was like, this is happening.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 1:15 PM\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 There's so much waiting in this entire process. Just getting ready.\par \par \uc2 JANE (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I had one of the most amazing nurses.\par \par \uc2 JANE (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 My name is Jane, and I'm a nurse. And I'm gonna help you get ready for your procedure today.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 She was so sweet and kind.\par \par \uc2 JANE (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 And your pulse is a little fast, which makes sense, because you're probably...\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 She went through everything, step by step.\par \par \uc2 JANE (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 Then the two little white pills, one of them is (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Making sure that we knew what was going on.\par \par \uc2 JANE (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 The other one is Vistaril, which will help a little bit with the anxiety. I'm gonna have you sit in here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 1:30 PM\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 After I changed into the robe, I waited about 30 minutes before they give me the medication that started the process. Started the waiting game.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 1:45 PM\par \par \uc2 JANE (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 Would you like a magazine to look at, or anything?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. I just sat and watched the clock, wishing that the time would go by faster. I just had the medicine for thinning out the cervix and dilating it. I have to sit and wait an hour to an hour and a half before they'll check and see if I'm ready for them to perform the procedure.\par \par \uc2 STAFF (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Do you feel secure in your decision today?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. My decision hasn't wavered. It's my body, and it's my choice. I don't think it's right for people to try and convince others when it's not their life that's about to change. No one talks about this process. They don't talk about how it starts, what medicines you take, and what is the expectation and the timeframe. I'm glad that I'm able to kind of shine a light and give people a little sense of control back that I feel like I've been lacking in this process. Waiting for my turn to go into the room was so heavy, because you're sitting there knowing that there's a girl in there before you, watching her come out, seeing that thumbs-up from her that she was doing okay after it, that put a little bit of ease on my nerves.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 The most comforting part during that entire process was being able to ask them questions. I asked them, once the procedure had started, how much longer of this? And immediately they said, this much longer. Only a couple more minutes. You're doing amazing. And then finally hearing, "We're done. It's over."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 4:45 PM\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I wanna go home.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 We got in the car. And we started making our way to the airport, got on the flight, and I finally slept.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 6:30 PM\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I looked out, and I was, like, "I'm home."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:00 PM\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I'm so close. I can put on comfy PJs and just go to bed. I'd just gotten home, and my mom looks at me and goes, "You will not believe what I was just sent."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Breaking news, a federal judge has blocked enforcement of the Texas law, the most restrictive abortion law...\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Texas clinics resuming abortion services after a federal judge blocked the state's 6-week abortion ban from being enforced.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I just face-palmed. And I was just like, really? Like, now? Finally, after everything I went through?\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 The past 24 hours has been a whirlwind of emotion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Twenty-one-year-old Maddie, a Texas college student who traveled hundreds of miles ouch state to get an abortion, is back home recovering.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I have to kind of start collecting my thoughts on everything, and then just the relief after, that it was finally done.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But just as her personal journey is ending, the public fight is intensifying. At the same time Maddie's plane was landing back in Houston, the very law that forced her to go to Mississippi for her procedure was blocked.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Of course, the day of my procedure and finally getting home, we found out this huge news.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A federal judge calling Senate Bill 8 unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 To think that this could all just like be overturned again, and it goes back into place as soon as tomorrow really scares me.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And that's what happened. Just a day later, a federal appeals court allowed the ban to resume for now, while the \uc2 US Department of Justice\uc2  appeals. In the State Capitol, outside a Planned Parenthood clinic, prayers continue, as usual.\par \par \uc2 HEATHER GARDNER (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR CENTRAL TEXAS COALITION FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 I don't think that there's ever too early of a restriction on abortion, because no matter what, an abortion is taking a life, a human life.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For the last 10 years, Heather Gardner has trained what she calls sidewalk advocates to pray outside abortion facilities across the country. She says SB-8 has benefits, but she acknowledges that some Texans will find ways around the law.\par \par \uc2 HEATHER GARDNER (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR CENTRAL TEXAS COALITION FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 We're very well aware that women will go to other states to have abortions. We want women to not have to feel so desperate that they have to do that.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With all eyes on Texas right now, anti-abortion rights advocates are using the law as a rallying cry.\par \par \uc2 LILA ROSE (PRESIDENT LIVE ACTION)\par \par \uc2 Texas's law is historic. I mean, it is the most legal protection in effect right now across the country for human lives.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Lila Rose is the president of Live Action.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Do you hope that this becomes a blueprint for other states?\par \par \uc2 LILA ROSE (PRESIDENT LIVE ACTION)\par \par \uc2 I think that Texas's law should be an inspiration to other states, because they found an enforcement mechanism that allows the life-saving law to remain in effect. But I think the ultimate answer here is to set right the false precedent, the bad precedent of Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Critics of this law will say that women who want to get an abortion will find the means to do it. They will go out of state. They have proven to travel hundreds of miles to do it. Some critics even say that this may push women to perform illegal abortions on themselves.\par \par \uc2 LILA ROSE (PRESIDENT LIVE ACTION)\par \par \uc2 Well, there's a multifaceted problem, here. First of all, is our societal approach to pregnancy and motherhood, and seeing the preborn child as a threat or a risk or an enemy, as opposed to a precious member of the human family. And then we need to keep doing things like what Texas is doing with their abortion alternatives program. This is exactly what we should be focusing on, as opposed to promoting the death and destruction of children in the womb.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While the rest of the country is focused on Texas...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Your baby is not a mistake. Your baby is a gift from God.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...many advocates are watching that clinic in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Love your wife, love your girlfriend.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And the upcoming case in front of the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 LILA ROSE (PRESIDENT LIVE ACTION)\par \par \uc2 I think that the Supreme Court is very likely to at least chip away at the illogical and unjust precedent that Roe v. Wade has set. Roe v. Wade belongs in the trash heap of history with other unjust Supreme Court cases like Dred V. Scott (sic) that failed to acknowledge the humanity of a certain group of people.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Clinic director Shannon Brewer says, she will continue fighting to keep the doors open.\par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREWER (CLINIC DIRECTOR JACKSON WOMEN'S HEALTH ORGANIZATION)\par \par \uc2 I just feel good that they're able to come here. If I, as tired as we are sometimes, every day I get to wake and up say that again, I'm okay.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 I feel like this entire process of everything has happened for a reason. Everything happens in life for a reason, and it's my chance to speak on it.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Maddie tells us her parents helped pay for her procedure and the travel out of state. She knows many women don't have that kind of support.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 There were so many unneeded obstacles that I managed to get over, but many women won't. The fact that I called over 30 clinics, that speaks to how many women are affected by this. If that doesn't shock you, I don't know what will.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) As a parent, as her mother, looking forward, what are your hopes for your daughter?\par \par \uc2 PARENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 That she doesn't let anybody make her feel ashamed or that she's done anything wrong, because she hasn't. And I hope that she will fulfill her dream of being a mom when she's ready, when she is ready to become mom, and not any time before.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 My biggest thing is making sure that other women know that they're not alone. If Texas is gonna make this difficult, make it difficult for Texas. Don't go silently. And if they need an inspiration, I hope I can be that for them.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE: THE APPOINTMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: EACH YEAR, ABOUT 55,000 ABORTIONS TAKE PLACE IN TEXAS.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THROUGHOUT 2020, THE NUMBER OF TEXAS RESIDENTS SEEKING OUT-OF-STATE ABORTIONS DOUBLED.\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020211014ehad00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NIGHTLINE\b0\par\par\uc2 180 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Tonight...\par \par \uc2 JANE (NURSE)\par \par \uc2 So, you can just have a seat, right here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE APPOINTMENT\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 "The Appointment," an intimate journey, one young Texas woman...\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You didn't plan to be pregnant at this period of your life.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely not.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Sharing some of the most personal moments of her life, crossing state lines to have an abortion, and taking us with her inside the clinic.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (CROSSED STATE LINES TO GET AN ABORTION)\par \par \uc2 It's my body, and it's my choice.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 The restrictive new law at the epicenter of the battle.\par \par \uc2 HEATHER GARDNER (EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR CENTRAL TEXAS COALITION FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 No matter what, an abortion is taking a life, a human life.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Anti-abortion advocates hopeful they can change the law of the land.\par \par \uc2 LILA ROSE (PRESIDENT LIVE ACTION)\par \par \uc2 Roe v. Wade belongs in the trash heap of history. It's time for Roe to go.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 This special edition of "Nightline," "The Appointment," will be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020211014ehad00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CARE FOR THE CAREGIVERS COUPLE SHARES THEIR CANCER JOURNEY THROUGH PHOTOS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,076 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, EVACUATIONS, SAFETY\par \par \uc2 PLANE, CRASH, NELSON, KEELEY, RAY, PELLOTH\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, VACCINES, \uc2 SOUTHWEST AIRLINES\uc2 , JONES, MURRAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOUTHWEST CANCELLATIONS CHAOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGERS LEFT STRANDED AFTER AIRLINE SCRAPS THOUSANDS OF FLIGHTS\par \par \uc2 CANCELLATIONS, KELLY, \uc2 SOUTHWEST AIRLINES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOUTHWEST CEO ON CANCELLATIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PASSENGERS LEFT STRANDED AFTER AIRLINE SCRAPS THOUSANDS OF FLIGHTS\par \par \uc2 TOEBBE, INVESTIGATION, BANNAT, SUBMARINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACCUSED SUBMARINE SPIES DUE IN COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NAVY ENGINEER & WIFE CHARGED WITH TRYING TO SELL U.S. MILITARY SECRETS\par \par \uc2 RAMIREZ, SAFETY, NUNEZ, HAFLIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEARTWARMING HOMECOMING FOR TEXAS 3-YEAR-OLD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RELEASED FROM HOSPITAL AFTER MIRACULOUS RESCUE\par \par \uc2 BOSTON, BASEBALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 RED SOX\uc2  CLINCH DIVISION SERIES WITH WALKOFF WIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOSTON BEATS TAMPA BAY TO ADVANCE TO ALCS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 DISCRIMINATION, GRUDEN, RESIGNATION, ROSMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JON GRUDEN OUT AS RAIDERS COACH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESIGNS AMID SCANDAL OVER PAST RACIST & HOMOPHOBIC EMAILS\par \par \uc2 MARROW, RESCUE, MANHOLE, ACCIDENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HERO MOM SPEAKS OUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMAN WHO JUMPED INTO OPEN MANHOLE TO SAVE TODDLER TELLS HER STORY\par \par \uc2 QR CODES, SCAM, OSTROWSKI, SAFETY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING ABOUT QR CODES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW SCAMMERS MAY BE CREATING FAKE ONES TO STEAL YOUR MONEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, EVACUATIONS, SAFETY\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, FDA, BOOSTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE BOOSTERS ON THE WAY?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FDA PANEL TO MEET ON ADDITIONAL DOSES OF MODERNA & J&J VACCINES\par \par \uc2 AMAZON, WORK, HOME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON EXTENDS WORK-FROM-HOME POLICY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MORE EMPLOYERS OFFERING FLEXIBILITY TO RETAIN EMPLOYEES\par \par \uc2 "WONKA", CHALAMET, PLATE STASH, JORDAN, AUCTION, ICKY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POP NEWS\par \par \uc2 LEGO, STEREOTYPES, DI NONNO\par \par \uc2 DIABETES, HEALTH, NEINSTEIN, BLOOD SUGAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRACKING YOUR BLOOD SUGAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CAN GLUCOSE MONITORS HELP US STOP SABOTAGING OUR NUTRITION GOALS?\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, RATHKOPF, BROWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CARE FOR THE CAREGIVERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUPLE SHARES THEIR CANCER JOURNEY THROUGH PHOTOS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Now to Breast Cancer Awareness Month. This morning, we're sharing a story of how therapy and some incredibly powerful photos helped one husband find his inner strength to support his family through his wife's difficult diagnosis. Erielle Reshef is here with more on caring for caregivers. Good morning, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Hey, good morning to you, Michael. The Rathkopfs documented every step of their experience. Nothing was off-limits. Their photos capturing hope and heartache from a caregiver's perspective.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just two weeks after her 37th birthday, Anna Rathkopf heard the news she never imagined. The mom of then two-and-a-half-year-old Jesse was diagnosed with stage 1 triple positive breast cancer, an aggressive form of the disease.\par \par \uc2 ANNA RATHKOPF (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I felt like the earth opened and I'm just in freefall.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Anna and her husband Jordan were facing a daunting new reality.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) You pretty quickly had to pivot from husband and father to caregiver.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN RATHKOPF (HUSBAND & CAREGIVER)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I mean, I did have to help a lot. She was just so weak.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jordan says, he often felt powerless as he tried to balance supporting Anna while keeping life stable for their son.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN RATHKOPF (HUSBAND & CAREGIVER)\par \par \uc2 I had severe anxiety. We went to ask the social worker if there was a support group and they thought we meant for her and I was like, no, no, for me. And it felt like I was barely getting by.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, to find strength, the photographer professor picked up his camera.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN RATHKOPF (HUSBAND & CAREGIVER)\par \par \uc2 We felt like our story hadn't been told in this way. We couldn't find anything quite like it of a young family living through cancer.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The raw images reflecting the highs and lows. Snapshots of snow angels, candid moments cuddling with Jesse, and that day Anna decided to shave her head.\par \par \uc2 ANNA RATHKOPF (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 It was helping us emotionally.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Those photos are incredibly moving. What do they mean now?\par \par \uc2 ANNA RATHKOPF (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I sometimes feel like before and after. As I'm trying to connect to the before, I want to connect to the person that I was before.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jordan eventually compiled the collection into a powerful photo essay hoping their images raise awareness about the cancer journey for patients and their caregivers.\par \par \uc2 JORDAN RATHKOPF (HUSBAND & CAREGIVER)\par \par \uc2 I think what worked for me to get through this was to admit I needed help and I was literally hanging on by a thread. I would just go to my car and cry for hours because I didn't want anyone else to see me. And once I started getting therapy and medication, I felt like I was actually in a better place to help take care of my family because I was able to take better care of myself.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Research shows 50% of cancer caregivers reported high emotional stress, 43% say they needed help to manage it.\par \par \uc2 SUSAN BROWN (SR DIR HEALTH INFORMATION & PUBLICATIONS SUSAN G KOMEN)\par \par \uc2 Talking with friends, professionals or others who have been through this experience or who are going through the similar experience can be very helpful. But really the best way to take care of a loved one is for caregivers to take care of themselves.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Do you live your life differently now?\par \par \uc2 JORDAN RATHKOPF (HUSBAND & CAREGIVER)\par \par \uc2 It changed the direction of our lives. It's brought us together. It's just cemented everything we knew was there.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And I'm happy to report that Anna is now healthy and in remission. Jordan says caregiving often meant fulfilling tasks that might seem small like answering Anna's phone when the doctors would call because she was too nervous to get the news by herself. The Rathkopfs' touching photos are now showcased on the Susan G. Komen blog. Guys?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Great story.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And, you know, I love the support for those who are supporting their family. When we come back, Victoria Beckham is gonna be here live.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA CONCERT SERIES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THURSDAY LIAM PAYNE\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 "GMA" Thursday, say good morning, sunshine, to Liam Payne performing for you. Thursday only on "Good Morning America," sponsored by...\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211027ehac0000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION BAN BATTLE FEDERAL APPEALS COURT REINSTATES TEXAS LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 332 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HALLOWEEN GREEN LIGHT\par \par \uc2 COVID, MERCK, PILL, FDA, MANDATES, FAUCI\par \par \uc2 SOUTHWEST, FLIGHTS, CANCELATIONS, PASSENGERS\par \par \uc2 SUBMARINE, TOEBBE, SECRETS, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , STING, ARREST\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, COURTS, LAW, TEXAS\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Well George, now to the latest on the battle over the Texas abortion law, the most restrictive in the nation. A federal appeals court reinstated that law after a lower court put it on hold, and now it's up to the Justice Department to make the next move. Senior national correspondent Terry Moran has the latest from Washington for us. Good morning, Terry.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BAN BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL APPEALS COURT REINSTATES TEXAS LAW AFTER IT WAS PUT ON HOLD\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, Amy. That's right, women in Texas are again facing a denial of their rights under the constitution as this battle in court continues. And it's been such a roller coaster. Last week a federal judge blocked that law from going into effect, that Texas law which bans abortions after six weeks, that amounts to a near-total ban on abortions in the state. The judge in that case calling it the law, quote, "An offensive depravation of an important constitutional right."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BAN BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTICE DEPARTMENT SET TO RESPOND AFTER FEDERAL APPEALS COURT REINSTATES LAW\par \par \uc2 TERRY MORAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) But then two days later late Friday, a federal appeals court reinstated the law and gave the Biden Justice Department until tomorrow to respond to that ruling. All this back and forth and uncertainty as shuttered most clinics in Texas, and driven women into neighboring states. Some driving hundreds of miles and thousands of, spending thousands of dollars. And this case will certainly go to the Supreme Court. But that could take weeks, at least. Amy.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, Terry Moran with the latest from Washington for us. Thank you, Terry. T.J.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211026ehab0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS ABORTION BATTLE DOJ TO RESPOND TO APPEALS COURT REINSTATING LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FOUND ALIVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW OVERNIGHT: MISSING THREE-YEAR-OLD BOY FOUND ALIVE\par \par \uc2 RAMIREZ, SAMARITAN, JARVIS, SOWELL\par \par \uc2 AIRPLANE, PASSENGER, TARMAC, KUNKLE, KHUJA\par \par \uc2 VACCINE, MANDATES, SEATTLE, \uc2 COPS\uc2 , PATRICK, VILLANUEVA\par \par \uc2 TWINDEMIC, COVID, FLU, MORITA\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, ABORTION, APPEALS, MILLER, FLORES, MCGILL JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Now to what's next in the battle over that restrictive abortion law in Texas. The Justice Department has until Tuesday to respond to an appeals court ruling that allows the law to remain in place after a lower court temporarily blocked it. So let's go to White House correspondent Maryalice Parks. She is live at the White House right now with much more on all this. Maryalice, good morning.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, Gio. Healthcare experts say that all of this ping-ponging in the courts has left doctors and patients frustrated, confused, and totally in the lurch.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, whiplash for patients and doctors in Texas.\par \par \uc2 AMY HAGSTROM MILLER\uc2  (PRESIDENT AND CEO WHOLE WOMAN'S HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 There's a lot of anguish, a lot of pain, desperation.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Reproductive health advocates protesting after the conservative 5th Circuit Court of Appeals reinstated the highly-restrictive abortion law that went into effect in Texas last month.\par \par \uc2 AMY HAGSTROM MILLER\uc2  (PRESIDENT AND CEO WHOLE WOMAN'S HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 We had to cancel appointments. Many patients start to beg the staff. People shouldn't be begging for healthcare services.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The law allows people to bring lawsuits against someone they think helped facilitate an abortion after around six weeks into the pregnancy, before most women even know they are pregnant. The fact that it's enforced by average citizens makes it incredibly complicated for the courts.\par \par \uc2 SARAH ISGUR FLORES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) The Supreme Court has never actually had to deal with before, whether these so-called bounty laws that - this one happens to be on abortion, but could be on gun rights or on religious freedom - whether they will pass constitutional muster.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Just last week, a lower court had put the law on pause, but less than two days after that abrupt turnaround, this new order banning more abortions in the state once again, anti-abortion advocates calling it a victory. The Justice Department is challenging the law. The court says it has until Tuesday to make its next move. The head of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  telling us they're supporting patients who now want to try to travel out of the state to get abortion care.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS MCGILL JOHNSON\uc2  (PRES AND CEO PLANNED PARENTHOOD FEDERATION OF AMERICA)\par \par \uc2 We have a patient who traveled from Texas to Aurora, Colorado, over 1,000 miles. And this patient traveled by herself because she was so afraid that if anyone traveled with her, that they could be charged with supporting an abortion.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It is likely the Supreme Court will eventually weigh in on the merits and substance of that Texas law. But coming up soon in December, the Supreme Court will also hear arguments around another law out of Mississippi. This is a more traditional abortion law that bans most abortions after 15 weeks. Experts watching that one closely, too. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah, so many watching that closely. Maryalice Parks, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211026ehaa00006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS ABORTION LAW WHIPLASH FEDERAL APPEALS COURT TEMPORARILY REINSTATES BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS STRANDED AT THE AIRPORT\par \par \uc2 SOUTHWEST, FLIGHTS, CANCELATIONS, PASSENGERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS STRANDED AT THE AIRPORT\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, THREATS, WINDS, HAIL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SIGNIFICANT TORNADO THREAT\par \par \uc2 VACCINE, MANDATES, VILLANUEVA, FUDA, MILITARY, FAUCI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VACCINE MANDATE BATTLES\par \par \uc2 CAPITOL, INSURRECTION, TRUMP, SUBPOENAS, COMMISSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW JANUARY 6TH DETAILS\par \par \uc2 VIDEO, ARREST, PARAPLEGIC, POLICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POLICE RELEASE ARREST VIDEO\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, MILLER, JOHNSON, COURTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION LAW WHIPLASH\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Elwyn, thanks so much. Next to Texas, where the legal back-and-forth over the highly restrictive abortion law is just getting started. An appeals court has now reinstated the law, which effectively bans most abortions in the state. This comes nearly 48 hours after a judge had halted it. This means women in Texas who want an abortion after six weeks now have to travel out of state. Here's ABC's White House correspondent, MaryAlice Parks.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION LAW WHIPLASH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL APPEALS COURT TEMPORARILY REINSTATES BAN\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, with the nation's most restrictive abortion ban back in effect for now, health care providers again forced to turn away patients.\par \par \uc2 AMY HAGSTROM MILLER (PRES AND CEO WHOLE WOMEN'S HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 There's a lot of anguish, a lot of pain, desperation.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The 5th circuit federal court of appeals temporarily reinstating the ban just two days after a lower court had paused the law.\par \par \uc2 ALEXIS MCGILL JOHNSON\uc2  (PRES AND CEO PLANNED PARENTHOOD)\par \par \uc2 We've had patients who thought they could maybe get into a clinic in the state, and now, after the ruling, will have to figure out how to travel again.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) On Wednesday, after the law was halted, some providers say they did open their doors for abortion services. But now they could be in legal jeopardy for doing so. Anti-abortion advocates calling the latest court order a victory.\par \par \uc2 CHRISTINE ARROYO (COALITION FOR LIFE)\par \par \uc2 We're out here to help the women make a better choice for their lives.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Not only does the law ban abortions after around six weeks, before most women even know they are pregnant, but it also allows average citizens to bring a lawsuit against someone they think helped facilitate the abortion. That fact has made it harder for the Biden administration to challenge the law in court.\par \par \uc2 SARAH ISGUR FLORES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Who do you sue when the law empowers every citizen in the United States to be able to bring this lawsuit?\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Department of Justice now has until Tuesday to make their next legal move.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And, Linsey, it is likely the Supreme Court will eventually weigh in on the merits of that Texas law. And in December, the new conservative majority on the bench here will face its first major test on abortion, with another case from Mississippi that directly asks the justice to consider overturning Roe V. Wade. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020211011ehaa00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WRAPPING BREAST CANCER PATIENTS IN HOPE NON-PROFIT SHARES SCARVES AND SUPPORT\b0\par\par\uc2 849 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAME CHANGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY TRAVEL SURGE\par \par \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , CHILDREN, VACCINE, FDA, CDC, BROWNSTEIN, BESSER\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, HOLIDAYS, TRAVEL, VACCINATED, PRICES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, FALLOUT, PITMAN, MILLER\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, SENATE, GOP, DEMS\par \par \uc2 OIL SPILL, PIPELINE, INVESTIGATION, CLEANUP\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FRAUD, INSURANCE, STRAUSS, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS, AROZARENA, HISTORIC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOODING RAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM OSCARS\par \par \uc2 LAUNDRIE, MANHUNT, PETITO, DEPAUL, RESNICK\par \par \uc2 GREAT WHITE, SHARK, STEINLEY, DAVIS, BADER\par \par \uc2 BOND, "NO TIME TO DIE", CRAIG, BOX OFFICE, NOVAK\par \par \uc2 PEPI, SOCCER, WORLD CUP\par \par \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , FDA, VACCINE, CHILDREN, AUTHORIZATION\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BATTLE, BAN, LAW, FEDERAL, JUDGE, TEXAS\par \par \uc2 MAIL, USPS, SLOW\par \par \uc2 ADELE, DIVORCE, WEIGHT LOSS, NNADI, HATTERSLEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 TREND, RETAIL, PAY LATER, HOLIDAYS, HERZOG\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 CHIPPENDALES, MURDER, GREED\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, SCARVES, HOPE, MACGREGOR\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Now to breast cancer awareness month this morning. The story of how the power of friendship during one woman's valiant fight against breast cancer at just 30 years old inspired a global sisterhood with hope scarves. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Lara MacGregor was just 30 and two months away from welcoming her second child when she was diagnosed with breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 LARA MACGREGOR (FOUNDER HOPE SCARVES)\par \par \uc2 I had four rounds of chemotherapy while I was pregnant. I went from doing everything I could to have the healthiest pregnancy to just pumping toxic chemicals into my veins.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) During her grueling treatment, she received a gift, a simple gesture that would change everything.\par \par \uc2 LARA MACGREGOR (FOUNDER HOPE SCARVES)\par \par \uc2 A friend of a friend named Kelly sent me a box of scarves with a note that said, you can do this, and it was just inspiring, knowing this other young woman had faced cancer, had come through her treatments and was passing them on to me.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After delivering a healthy baby boy, Lara went into remission and launched Hope Scarves, collecting scarves from cancer survivors around the world and passing them on to others battling the disease.\par \par \uc2 LARA MACGREGOR (FOUNDER HOPE SCARVES)\par \par \uc2 This community has truly become what I like to call "The Sisterhood of The Traveling Scarves."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE STORY OF HOPE SCARVES. ONE WOMAN'S MISSION TO SPREAD LIGHT IN THE FACE OF DARKNESS\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Hope Scarves sharing nearly 20,000 scarves worldwide.\par \par \uc2 HOPE SCARF RECIPIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Getting a Hope Scarf is like getting a beautiful hug.\par \par \uc2 HOPE SCARF RECIPIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I wore it throughout my treatment.\par \par \uc2 HOPE SCARF RECIPIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I was always reminded that I was not alone.\par \par \uc2 HOPE SCARF RECIPIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It was a reminder that there was another young, tough mom who had made it through these really tough treatments.\par \par \uc2 HOPE SCARF RECIPIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It was a way to start to move up a mountain that I was struggling to even acknowledge.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But seven years after her initial diagnosis, Lara's cancer returned and was now metastatic, spreading to other parts of her body. Nearly 30 percent of women with early stage breast cancer will develop metastatic disease.\par \par \uc2 LARA MACGREGOR (FOUNDER HOPE SCARVES)\par \par \uc2 The face of breast cancer that you often see of this happy, joyful survivor is very different than the reality for me and for thousands of other people with metastatic disease. Once you become metastatic, there's no end to treatment.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now 44 years old, Lara putting the spotlight on the not often told metastatic story...\par \par \uc2 HOPE SCARF RECIPIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I am a metastatic breast cancer patient.\par \par \uc2 HOPE SCARF RECIPIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I was metastatic, stage 4 right from the beginning when I was 29 years old.\par \par \uc2 HOPE SCARF RECIPIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Lara's hopeful spirit lifted me up.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...raising $1.5 million for research. With each Hope Scarf shared, Lara's mission to spread light in the face of darkness continues.\par \par \uc2 LARA MACGREGOR (FOUNDER HOPE SCARVES)\par \par \uc2 A hopeful life is not about living a life free of pain or sadness or fear, it's about learning how to hold both fear and joy in the same hand at the same time.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It is so important, this side of this, this journey that Lara is sharing. And she said something really beautiful after she was diagnosed with metastatic breast cancer, she said that she stopped saying that she is living life after cancer, she now says she lives life over cancer. And it reminds me of what we've heard Amy and Robin here say so much, you're not just surviving, you're, you're thriving.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Wow.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) A lot of wisdom there.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) A lot of wisdom, yeah. Really important, so we thank her for that story.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We're going to shift gears. Coming up, everybody, "No Time to Die" star Lea Seydoux joins us live.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORY SYNOPSES\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211025eha80000n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION BAN BATTLE FALLOUT AFTER FEDERAL JUDGE BLOCKS TEXAS LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAME CHANGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY TRAVEL SURGE\par \par \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , CHILDREN, VACCINE, FDA, CDC, BROWNSTEIN, BESSER\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, HOLIDAYS, TRAVEL, VACCINATED, PRICES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, FALLOUT, PITMAN, MILLER\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, SENATE, GOP, DEMS\par \par \uc2 OIL SPILL, PIPELINE, INVESTIGATION, CLEANUP\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FRAUD, INSURANCE, STRAUSS, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS, AROZARENA, HISTORIC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOODING RAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM OSCARS\par \par \uc2 LAUNDRIE, MANHUNT, PETITO, DEPAUL, RESNICK\par \par \uc2 GREAT WHITE, SHARK, STEINLEY, DAVIS, BADER\par \par \uc2 BOND, "NO TIME TO DIE", CRAIG, BOX OFFICE, NOVAK\par \par \uc2 PEPI, SOCCER, WORLD CUP\par \par \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , FDA, VACCINE, CHILDREN, AUTHORIZATION\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BATTLE, BAN, LAW, FEDERAL, JUDGE, TEXAS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We're going to turn now to the latest on the abortion rights battle that is playing out in Texas, all the fallout from the federal judge's decision to block enforcement of the most restrictive ban in the nation. Let's go back to Rachel Scott in Houston. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) George, good morning. That federal judge ruling that the Texas law banning abortions roughly six weeks into a woman's pregnancy is "flagrantly unconstitutional," but even with that ruling only a handful of clinics are resuming abortion procedures this morning. The rest say that they are not taking any chances and they are pointing to a unique part of this law that allows providers to be sued retroactively if the law is eventually reinstated. The Texas Attorney General says they will be challenging this, he plans to appeal to the 5th Circuit, that is known to be one of the most conservative courts in the nation. This likely to land in front of the Supreme Court. George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Thank you very much, Rachel. T.J.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211025eha80000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 711 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAME CHANGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY TRAVEL SURGE\par \par \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , CHILDREN, VACCINE, FDA, CDC, BROWNSTEIN, BESSER\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, HOLIDAYS, TRAVEL, VACCINATED, PRICES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, FALLOUT, PITMAN, MILLER\par \par \uc2 DEBT CEILING, SENATE, GOP, DEMS\par \par \uc2 OIL SPILL, PIPELINE, INVESTIGATION, CLEANUP\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , FRAUD, INSURANCE, STRAUSS, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS, AROZARENA, HISTORIC\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOODING RAIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM OSCARS\par \par \uc2 LAUNDRIE, MANHUNT, PETITO, DEPAUL, RESNICK\par \par \uc2 GREAT WHITE, SHARK, STEINLEY, DAVIS, BADER\par \par \uc2 BOND, "NO TIME TO DIE", CRAIG, BOX OFFICE, NOVAK\par \par \uc2 PEPI, SOCCER, WORLD CUP\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM. \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  has requested emergency use authorization for their COVID-19 vaccine for ages 5 to 11, nearly 30 million kids eligible if approved. The latest on that this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW FALLOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION RIGHTS BATTLE\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Abortion rights battle. The fallout after a federal judge blocks enforcement of the most restrictive abortion ban in the country. What could happen next.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ADELE'S VOGUE TAKE OVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STAR'S NEW MUSIC, MOTHERHOOD AND GETTING STRONG\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 For the first time ever, two fabulous "Vogues," one phenomenal cover star. Adele, her first interviews in five years on getting through her year of anxiety, getting strong, motherhood, divorce, and her new love. Telling it all as she gears up for the world to hear her side of the story in her self-redemption record.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUY NOW, PAY LATER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA CONSUMER ALERT\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Buy now, pay later. The big name retailers adopting the new shopping plan just in time for the holidays. The pitfalls you need to watch out for before you stock up on gifts.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WRAPPING UP HOPE\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Wrapping up hope. How the power of friendship during one woman's valiant fight against breast cancer inspired a global initiative, launching what she calls a "Sisterhood of The Traveling Scarves."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINALLY!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOND STAR LEA SEYBOUX LIVE ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And "No Time To Die" hits the big screen with a bang. This morning, the woman making bond history joins us live...\par \par \uc2 LEA SEYDOUX ("NO TIME TO DIE")\par \par \uc2 Why would I betray you?\par \par \uc2 DANIEL CRAIG ("NO TIME TO DIE")\par \par \uc2 We all have our secrets. We just didn't get to yours yet.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 ...as Daniel Craig's final bow breaks records. And we're saying good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, America. Hope you're doing well this Friday morning. It's going to be a busy morning here in Times Square. We're going to have the cast of "Phantom" kicking off our weekend with a live performance right here in Times Square. There they are. We are looking forward to that.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Very excited about that one. Also excited about being at the Cotton Bowl Stadium in Dallas this morning where they are gearing up for "College GameDay." It is one of the biggest rivalries in college football. If I've told you once, T.J., I've told you twice, Oklahoma and Texas.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yes, all right. But we need to all, of course here, George, say happy anniversary to Cecilia...\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah, she just showed me.\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...it's almost ten years to the day that she made her first appearance on "Good Morning America." There she is.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) This just popped up on my phone and I, in my own defense, have no recollection of ever having had a mullet, thank you very much.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What are you so concerned about?\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I was terrified. I was - look at the white knuckled grasp on my own hands I had. You guys were very sweet, as you still are to this day and I'm...\par \par \uc2 T.J. HOLMES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) That's great.\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...glad to be a part of this family. It's been a fun ten years, which makes me 21.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211025eha80000f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION BAN BATTLE FALLOUT AFTER FEDERAL JUDGE BLOCKS TEXAS LAW\b0\par\par\uc2 628 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GAME CHANGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY TRAVEL SURGE\par \par \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , CHILDREN, VACCINE, FDA, CDC, BROWNSTEIN, BESSER\par \par \uc2 TRAVEL, HOLIDAYS, TRAVEL, VACCINATED, PRICES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BAN, FALLOUT, PITMAN, MILLER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Okay, T.J., thanks. We're gonna get the latest now on the abortion rights battle playing out in Texas. All the fallout from the federal judge's decision to block enforcement of the most restrictive abortion ban in the nation. Rachel Scott is in Houston with a look at what could happen next. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BAN BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FALLOUT AFTER FEDERAL JUDGE BLOCKS ENFORCEMENT OF RESTRICTIVE TEXAS LAW\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) George, good morning. And the state of Texas already appealing this decision, so as it makes its way through the courts, some providers here in Texas tell me they are not taking any chances, holding off on resuming abortion procedures.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, just 24 hours after a federal judge halted the most restrictive abortion law in the nation, only a handful of clinics are taking the risk to resume procedures.\par \par \uc2 AMY HAGSTROM MILLER\uc2  (FOUNDER WHOLE WOMAN'S HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 We reached out to some of the patients that we had on a waiting list to come in to have abortions today.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Judge \uc2 Robert Pitman\uc2  ruled the law banning abortions as early as six weeks into pregnancy, was "Flagrantly unconstitutional." But the decision does not give providers blanket protection. They can still be sued retroactively if courts eventually determine the law should be enforced again, leaving the majority of providers waiting on the sidelines. For weeks Texas women like Maddie, a 21-year-old college student, have traveled hundreds of miles for an abortion. We sat down the day before her procedure in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) At six weeks you didn't even know you were pregnant?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (21-YEARS-OLD)\par \par \uc2 Not even close. I was still living my life as regular and as carefree of a college kid as I could be.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Maddie tells me she was on birth control. When she visited the doctor she thought she could only be a few weeks pregnant and under that six-week legal limit.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (21-YEARS-OLD)\par \par \uc2 When she told me that I was measuring at 10 1/2 weeks, I just cried. I was heartbroken and terrified because I felt like the only option that I knew I had was gone.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She started calling around to clinics in nearby states.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) How many clinics would you say you called altogether?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (21-YEARS-OLD)\par \par \uc2 Easily 30 if not more.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And most of them were booked?\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (21-YEARS-OLD)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She finally got an appointment in Mississippi, an option she knows others may not be able to afford. This morning she hopes Texas women who want the procedure won't have to go out of state to get it.\par \par \uc2 MADDIE (21-YEARS-OLD)\par \par \uc2 It's frustrating that it took so long for them to figure out that this is unconstitutional. Like this is a woman's right to have this option.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So the majority of clinics here in Texas are taking this wait and see approach. They received a surge in calls after that ruling and they do see it as an important step, but they tell me it's still clouded in so much uncertainty. George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah, this one is headed to the Supreme Court. Okay, Rachel, thanks very much. Cecilia.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211025eha800004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FEDERAL JUDGE BLOCKS ENFORCEMENT OF TEXAS ABORTION LAW "OFFENSIVE DEPRIVATION OF SUCH AN IMPORTANT RIGHT"\b0\par\par\uc2 565 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ABORTION, LAW, SUSPENSION, TEXAS, APPEAL\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SIMPKINS, SCHOOL, HARRISON, KOLBYE\par \par \uc2 OIL SPILL, INVESTIGATION, WILSHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW IMAGES OF CRACKED OIL PIPELINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWS RUPTURE THAT CAUSED UP TO, 144,000 GALLONS OF OIL TO SPILL\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, MANDATES, VACCINES, FLU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES VACCINE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CITY ENACTS ONE OF NATION'S STRICTEST MANDATES\par \par \uc2 DEBT, DEAL, SENATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK FROM THE BRINK?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE NEARS DEAL TO AVERT GOVERNMENT DEFAULT\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILD CARD WALKOFF!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DODGERS BEAT CARDINALS WITH GAME-WINNING HOME RUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, INVESTIGATION, BLAND\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, COLLEGE ADMISSIONS, WILSON, ABDELAZIZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JURY DELIBERATIONS BEGIN IN VARSITY BLUES TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRET AUDIO RECORDINGS FROM CASE REVEALED\par \par \uc2 HOME, HEATING, PRICES, WOLFE, TIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOME HEATING COST WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLS COULD RISE BY AT LEAST 30% THIS WINTER\par \par \uc2 PARKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLOCKED\par \par \uc2 BLOCK, TEXAS, ABORTION, JUDGE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We have some news this morning, as well. We're going to start with the breaking news. A federal judge has blocked enforcement of the Texas law, the most restrictive abortion law in the nation. Rachel Scott is back with the latest. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) George, good morning. And abortion providers in Texas this morning are breathing a sigh of relief. The White House in a statement says this is a step forward, but acknowledging the fight is far from over.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION LAW SUSPENSION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, breaking news in the battle over abortion rights. A federal judge ruling the Texas ban on the procedure as early as six weeks into pregnancy was "flagrantly unconstitutional." In a scathing 113-page opinion, calling it an "offensive deprivation of an important right." The controversial and unprecedented law sparking outrage around the country...\par \par \uc2 PROTEST LEADER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Health care.\par \par \uc2 PROTEST LEADER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is...\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Health care.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...and all but blocking access to abortions in the state. The judge taking aim squarely at the Republicans who crafted the law, accusing them of "contriving an unprecedented and transparent" scheme by making it harder for the courts to knock down the law by deputizing private citizens to sue anyone who aids and abets an unlawful abortion, from the doctors who perform them to the drivers who take women to the clinic. Those citizens could then collect a reward of at least $10,000. Overnight, the state of Texas filing an appeal leaving some providers hesitant to offer abortions again, fearing they might be sued retroactively if the law is reinstated.\par \par \uc2 STEVE SHELLIST (ATTORNEY)\par \par \uc2 I don't think it's going to just open up the doors and providers are going to start providing abortions, but I think many will still wait and see what the higher courts have to say.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) For weeks, some women have been traveling hundreds of miles to get an abortion procedure. Some clinics in Texas this morning do plan to resume procedures for women who are up to 18 weeks pregnant, but other clinics are planning on holding off, waiting to see how this all plays out in the courts. Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Many are. Okay, Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211023eha70000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THRIVERS TURNED ENTREPRENEURS INNOVATIVE PRODUCTS MADE BY BREAST CANCER SURVIVORS\b0\par\par\uc2 983 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ABORTION, LAW, SUSPENSION, TEXAS, APPEAL\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SIMPKINS, SCHOOL, HARRISON, KOLBYE\par \par \uc2 OIL SPILL, INVESTIGATION, WILSHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW IMAGES OF CRACKED OIL PIPELINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWS RUPTURE THAT CAUSED UP TO, 144,000 GALLONS OF OIL TO SPILL\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, MANDATES, VACCINES, FLU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES VACCINE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CITY ENACTS ONE OF NATION'S STRICTEST MANDATES\par \par \uc2 DEBT, DEAL, SENATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK FROM THE BRINK?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE NEARS DEAL TO AVERT GOVERNMENT DEFAULT\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILD CARD WALKOFF!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DODGERS BEAT CARDINALS WITH GAME-WINNING HOME RUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, INVESTIGATION, BLAND\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, COLLEGE ADMISSIONS, WILSON, ABDELAZIZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JURY DELIBERATIONS BEGIN IN VARSITY BLUES TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRET AUDIO RECORDINGS FROM CASE REVEALED\par \par \uc2 HOME, HEATING, PRICES, WOLFE, TIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOME HEATING COST WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLS COULD RISE BY AT LEAST 30% THIS WINTER\par \par \uc2 PARKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLOCKED\par \par \uc2 BLOCK, TEXAS, ABORTION, JUDGE\par \par \uc2 HALLOWEEN, SUPPLY, ISSUES, SHORTAGE\par \par \uc2 TURNER, CATALOG, QUARTER, ANNIVERSARY, DAWSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TINA TURNER SELLS MUSIC CATALOG\par \par \uc2 CURTIS, HOLLYWOOD, BEAUTY, PLASTIC SURGERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 THRIVERS, BREAST CANCER, ENTREPRENEUR\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Now to breast cancer awareness month. This morning, we are celebrating breast cancer thrivers turned entrepreneurs. They all saw a need, filled it with their innovative products for fellow thrivers. Amy is back with more on this. Hey, again, Amy.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Hey again to you, Robin. These three companies were all born out of cancer battles and their products are all things that the people behind them were looking for and couldn't find, so they knew other women going through breast cancer would want them too. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 2010, at just 28 years old, Dana's Donofree's breast cancer battle included a double mastectomy, chemo and radiation.\par \par \uc2 DANA DONOFREE (FOUNDER AND CEO ANAONO)\par \par \uc2 As I was going through all these surgeries I just realized, like, all of the ways I used to dress, the ways I used to express myself, beautiful lingerie, it just became not an option for me anymore. I was never prepared to, like, have my identity stripped away as a part of that process.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She searched for the perfect bra and couldn't find it so she started anaono.com a lingerie company tailored to breast cancer survivors of all surgeries and symmetries.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURVIVORS BUILDING BUSINESSES. INNOVATIVE PRODUCTS BY AND FOR BREAST CANCER SURVIVORS\par \par \uc2 DANA DONOFREE (FOUNDER AND CEO ANAONO)\par \par \uc2 Every bra is designed for two breasts and in our world we don't have that so to really support every surgery decision and outcome that comes from a cancer patient clientele was important to me.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dana offers bras to support mastectomy, reconstruction and radiation therapy, even post-surgery loungewear.\par \par \uc2 DANA DONOFREE (FOUNDER AND CEO ANAONO)\par \par \uc2 Thank you both for coming today.\par \par \uc2 DANA DONOFREE (FOUNDER AND CEO ANAONO)\par \par \uc2 We want people to feel beautiful and empowered in their own skin and their own surgery decisions and whatever that life has led them.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In 2009, breast cancer treatments caused Sonya Keshwani to lose her hair, and she says her quest for fashionable hair loss solutions was disappointing...\par \par \uc2 SONYA KESHWANI (FOUNDER STYLEESTEEM WARDROBE)\par \par \uc2 Everything I found online and in stores basically made me look and feel like a sick person.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ...so she started experimenting with fabrics and sewing patterns, creating turban designs she felt gave her back the confidence and dignity cancer stole.\par \par \uc2 SONYA KESHWANI (FOUNDER STYLEESTEEM WARDROBE)\par \par \uc2 They made getting dressed in the morning so much, so much more of a happier experience because I was able to coordinate different things with my outfit. I was able to dress up the way I used to before breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She wanted other women to have the same options, her turbans now available in some stores and online at styleesteem.com. Fashionable enough, says Sonya, to wear whether you've had hair loss from cancer or not. A lot of Lori Levine's stage II breast cancer battle was spent in the car on long rides to New York City for treatment. She would take on-the-go snacks like protein bars until a nutritionist said forget it.\par \par \uc2 LORI LEVINE (CO-FOUNDER SCOTT'S PROTEIN BALLS)\par \par \uc2 She said no more bars. They're, they're processed, they have chemicals. You can't eat them.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Enter husband Scott, a CFO in the tech world who was desperate to help out.\par \par \uc2 SCOTT LEVINE (CO-FOUNDER SCOTT'S PROTEIN BALLS)\par \par \uc2 You just need to be supportive at that point, right? So I spent time at night working on recipes and just ended up with a peanut butter chocolate chip protein ball that my wife loved.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He fine-tuned it to be a healthy, low calorie, low sugar, high protein snack that became quite popular around the neighborhood. They launched Scott's protein balls in four flavors that you can find online or in 30 stores in four states.\par \par \uc2 LORI LEVINE (CO-FOUNDER SCOTT'S PROTEIN BALLS)\par \par \uc2 Something good came out of something bad. You have to always look for a silver lining.\par \par \uc2 AMY ROBACH (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So inspirational. And by the way, all of these companies give back to the breast cancer community. The companies making the turbans and the bras both donate those products to women in need, and then Scott and Lori are planning to do events where they donate proceeds to breast cancer research. Robin, they are truly making their mess their message and helping others along the way.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And doing it beautifully. Amy, thank you. Now let's check in again with Rob. Rob.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211023eha70000k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 GOOD MORNING AMERICA\b0\par\par\uc2 615 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. Breaking news overnight in the battle over abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLOCKED\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Blocked. A federal judge stops enforcement of the new Texas abortion law, the most restrictive in the nation, banning nearly all abortions in the state. The reaction this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLASH FLOOD EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Also this morning, flash flood emergency. Millions in the southeast threatened. Ten inches of intense rain drenching Alabama.\par \par \uc2 RESCUER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm trying to get her out of the car. Water is rising.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The rescues underway right now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCHOOL SHOOTING NIGHTMARE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 School shooting nightmare. Gunfire erupting inside a Dallas-area high school.\par \par \uc2 STUDENT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I was definitely shaking. I was terrified.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Students locking themselves in classrooms. Four people wounded. The teen suspect now in custody.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRST VIDEO OF DAMAGED PIPELINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OIL SPILL DISASTER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 New overnight, the first video of the damaged pipeline blamed for the oil spill disaster off California. The Coast Guard investigation underway right now.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW VACCINE MANDATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVID CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 COVID crackdown. One of America's bigger cities announcing one of the toughest vaccine mandates affecting anyone going to bars, restaurants or the gym.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CDC DIRECTOR'S NEW WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLU SEASON FEARS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the new warning from the head of the CDC that the US is at risk of a severe flu season.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MURDAUGH MURDER MYSTERY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TWIST\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 New twist in that South Carolina double murder mystery. Alex Murdaugh, whose wife and son were killed in June, allegedly funneling millions of dollars from a wrongful death settlement to himself. Now, also being sued for allegedly stealing from his law firm.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUDIO RECORDINGS REVEALED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "VARSITY BLUES" TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The first trial in the "Varsity Blues" college admissions scandal heading to the jury. This morning, the audio recorded as part of the investigation between ringleader Rick Singer and the two millionaire parents.\par \par \uc2 RICK SINGER (ALLEGED RINGLEADER VARSITY BLUES SCANDAL)\par \par \uc2 I can send him your $500,000 that you wired into my account to secure the spot for one of your girls.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 What the tapes reveal.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW OVERNIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILD CARD WALKOFF!\par \par \uc2 SPORTS COMMENTATOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Swing and a drive.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And wild card walkoff.\par \par \uc2 SPORTS COMMENTATOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Walkoff. Walking off. Chris Taylor.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The Dodgers with ninth-inning fireworks after a nail-biter with the Cardinals, keeping the dream of a World Series repeat alive.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THURSDAY, OCTOBER 7TH, 2021\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "Good Morning America."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How exciting was that?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That was.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That was exciting. Good morning, America. We are glad you're with us on this busy Thursday morning. And what a finish. You know, you know it's a good finish because the LA fans did not leave early.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You noticed. That's true. They stayed for them.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And it paid off for them.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We have a lot of news to get to this morning. We're watching Capitol Hill, where they're hours away from a vote that could prevent a financial crisis. The deal does looks like it's coming together. We'll have all those details ahead.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211023eha700001\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FEDERAL JUDGE BLOCKS ENFORCEMENT OF TEXAS ABORTION LAW "OFFENSIVE DEPRIVATION OF SUCH AN IMPORTANT RIGHT"\b0\par\par\uc2 669 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ABORTION, LAW, SUSPENSION, TEXAS, APPEAL\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We will. But we're gonna with that breaking news overnight, a major development in the battle over abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL JUDGE BLOCKS ENFORCEMENT OF TEXAS ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RULES AGAINST "OFFENSIVE DEPRIVATION OF SCH AN IMPORTANT RIGHT"\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) A federal judge blocking enforcement of a Texas law, the most restrictive in the country. Our congressional correspondent Rachel Scott has the latest for us. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BAN BATTLE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Robin, good morning. And this was a blistering opinion. The judge saying, from the moment that this law went into effect, it has prevented women from exercising control over their own lives. The ruling handing the Biden administration legal victory, but the fight is far from over.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, breaking news in the battle over abortion rights. The most restrictive abortion law in the nation now suspended. A federal judge ruling the Texas ban on the procedure as early as six weeks into pregnancy was "flagrantly unconstitutional." In a scathing 113-page opinion, calling it an offensive deprivation of an important right. The controversial and unprecedented law sparking outrage around the country.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Health care.\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Abortion is?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Health care.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And all but blocking access to abortions in the state. We were there the day the law went into effect.\par \par \uc2 HEALTH CARE WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 She was surprised. She was distraught. And we began to explore options and think through the logistics if she would go out of state for the care that she needed.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Planned Parenthood said the number of patients at its Texas clinics plummeted by 80%, their call centers turned into crisis hotlines.\par \par \uc2 EMPLOYEE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 It has turned into a crisis center. People do not know where to go.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION LAW SUSPENSION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The judge taking aim squarely at the Republicans who crafted the law, accusing them of contriving an unprecedented and transparent scheme by making it harder for the courts to knock down the law by deputizing private citizens to sue anyone who aids and abets an unlawful abortion from the doctors who perform them, to the drivers who take women to the clinic. Those citizens could then collect a reward of at least $10,000. Overnight, the state of Texas filing an appeal, leaving some providers hesitant to offer abortions again, fearing they might be sued retroactively if the law is reinstated.\par \par \uc2 EXPERT (MALE)\par \par \uc2 I don't think it's gonna just open up the doors and providers are gonna start providing abortions, but I think many will still wait and see what the higher courts have to say.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Even the judge who blocked the law acknowledging another court could rule differently, but writing, "This court will not sanction one more day."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) In a statement, the White House calls this an important step forward, but they also acknowledge that the battle over abortion rights has only just begun. And the issue will land right here at the Supreme Court this fall, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So, what does this mean for women in Texas right now, Rachel?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Well, Robin, I can tell you I just got back from Texas. And I was speaking to women that have been traveling hundreds of miles for an abortion procedure. Some clinics this morning in Texas do plan to resume those abortion appointments for women who are up to 18 weeks pregnant, but other clinics are still hesitant, waiting for this to play out in the courts, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Okay, Rachel, thanks so much. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right, Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211023eha700002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 627 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ABORTION, LAW, SUSPENSION, TEXAS, APPEAL\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SIMPKINS, SCHOOL, HARRISON, KOLBYE\par \par \uc2 OIL SPILL, INVESTIGATION, WILSHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW IMAGES OF CRACKED OIL PIPELINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWS RUPTURE THAT CAUSED UP TO, 144,000 GALLONS OF OIL TO SPILL\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, MANDATES, VACCINES, FLU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES VACCINE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CITY ENACTS ONE OF NATION'S STRICTEST MANDATES\par \par \uc2 DEBT, DEAL, SENATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK FROM THE BRINK?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE NEARS DEAL TO AVERT GOVERNMENT DEFAULT\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILD CARD WALKOFF!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DODGERS BEAT CARDINALS WITH GAME-WINNING HOME RUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 MURDAUGH, INVESTIGATION, BLAND\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, COLLEGE ADMISSIONS, WILSON, ABDELAZIZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JURY DELIBERATIONS BEGIN IN VARSITY BLUES TRIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECRET AUDIO RECORDINGS FROM CASE REVEALED\par \par \uc2 HOME, HEATING, PRICES, WOLFE, TIPS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOME HEATING COST WARNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLS COULD RISE BY AT LEAST 30% THIS WINTER\par \par \uc2 PARKER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BLOCKED\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America. It's 8:00 AM. Breaking news overnight, a federal judge blocks the new Texas abortion law from being enforced. The law bans nearly all abortions in the state. The reaction this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S REALLY HAUNTING HALLOWEEN...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOPPING SCARE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Shopping scare. Halloween haunted by all those supply chain issues. Just three and a half weeks to trick-or-treat. Why the holiday could be more frightful than fun this fall.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "WIPING OUT GENERATIONS OF BEAUTY"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAMIE LEE CURTIS TAKES ON HOLLYWOOD\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The ugly truth about beauty standards. Actress Jamie Lee Curtis saying obsession with plastic surgery is wiping out generations of beauty and why she regrets the procedures she had in the past.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SURVIVORS TO THRIVERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INNOVATIVE PRODUCTS MADE BY BREAST CANCER SURVIVORS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 From survivors to thrivers to entrepreneurs.\par \par \uc2 LORI LEVINE (CO-FOUNDER SCOTT'S PROTEIN BALLS)\par \par \uc2 Something good came out of something bad. You have to always look for a silver lining.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How these women used their breast cancer journey to create innovative products to help themselves and others.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TINA TURNER'S \uc2 BLOCKBUSTER\uc2  DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "SIMPLY THE BEST"\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tina Turner's blockbuster deal. The legendary pop diva cashing in, selling her image and music rights. What she's saying this morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RISE & SHINE!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING FROM WISCONSIN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 "Rise & Shine" and good morning from Wisconsin, home to world champions, the \uc2 Milwaukee Bucks\uc2 ...\par \par \uc2 BALL PLAYER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 ...the \uc2 Green Bay Packers\uc2 ...\par \par \uc2 SPORTS COMMENTATOR (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Aaron Jones, touchdown, Packers.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 ...and everyday superheroes like the barber who kept his shop open to offer vaccines to his community. "GMA" taking you to the heart of America's dairy land.\par \par \uc2 KAREN KELLEY (KELLEY COUNTRY CREAMERY)\par \par \uc2 We've never shut our doors. We stayed open the entire time.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It's all ahead as we say...\par \par \uc2 RESIDENTS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, everybody. Glad you're starting your Thursday with us here on "GMA." And we are so excited to "Rise & Shine" in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We are. We're looking live at - well, we're looking live at that beautiful woman right there and also the, the Milwaukee Art Museum. The landmark is celebrating its 20th anniversary this month. It's just one of the places our Mona Kosar Abdi is taking us this morning. She is showing us all that America's dairy land has to offer and introducing us to the people helping that great state bounce back.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Looking forward to that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211023